********************************************************************************* Control Panel NDA 2.1** Copyright Apple Computer, Inc. 1991-1993* All Rights Reserved** by David A. Lyons, started 20-Jan-91********************************************************************************** REVISION HISTORY** Version 2.0 for System 6.0** 20-Jan-91 Dave Lyons*   Initial coding.  Took about 2.5 hours to get the shell working.*   The list of CDevs is hard-coded, and it cycles through to the*   next one each time you open the DA.  The battery-RAM updating*   is working, even!** 13..14-Feb-91 DAL*   Making this into a for-real alpha-quality thing so I can check it*   in soon.** 18-Feb-91 DAL*   Can I code on adrenaline?  Yes, I Think SO!  Not really alpha yet,*   but let's see what I can do in the next five hours...** 19-Feb-91 DAL*   Still Going (thud, thud, thud, thud).  Kinda works, in a minimal*   sort of way.** 20-Feb-91 DAL*   Successfully builds all its data structures in memory and displays*   the scrolling list of icons!** 21-Feb-91am DAL*   Really starting to cook now.  Might even work right with multiple*   CDevs open, even!  (Later...working good.)** 25-Feb-91am DAL*   Looks like this is going on the 6.0d26 build.  So let's fix it up*   some more, put in the About box and Help & stuff. **   Finished WhatAccessRequest routine, so we'll open things up read-only*   if we booted off of AppleShare.**   Kludged Run events for one window only, and got the data file stuff*   working.** === released on 6.0d26 ===** 26-Feb-91 DAL*   Dim out the About and Help buttons when there are no CDevs selected.*   Make the first CDev be selected by default.**   Uses VersionString to build version text from the rVersion resource.** 27-Feb-91 DAL*   Fixed Run events so they won't dispatch to a NIL or invalid window.*   Fixed GlobalToLocal and LocalToGlobal calls on rectangles!*   Now I use ResetMember2 instead of NextMember2 to scan for CDevs to*     open.  This way they are no longer selected when the open is done.*   Now puts up a watch cursor around opening CDevs.** 28-Feb-91 DAL (2.0d3)*   When calling HitCDEV for a nonextended control, I now pass $FFFFFFFF*   for the control ID.  Some existing CDevs were counting on getting a*   large value here, and I was passing zero before.**   Adding some better error handling.  Instead of crashing if there isn't*   enough memory, it just does nothing.** 2-Mar-91 DAL (2.0d4)*   Stripping leading blanks from CDev names in the list.** 3-Mar-91 DAL (2.0d4)*   We accept SendRequest($0F01) from MenuKey to implement Apple-ESC*     as our hotkey to open up the Control Panels window (will make*     this configurable later).  Hilites the first menu title around*     opening self.*   Centers CDev rectangles better vertically than before.*   Now sets the port to the CDev window during Create and Init messages.** 13-Mar-91 DAL (2.0d5)*   Was neglecting to invalidate an icon that was deselected, in the case*   that I got an error trying to open it.** 14-Mar-91 DAL*   Take a whack at the palette manager!** === released on 6.0d29 ===** 22-Mar-91 DAL (2.0d6)*   Control Panel's own resource fork is now opened read-only on*     AppleShare, so multiple users can use it.*   Tweaked the little palette manager so that UseStandardPalette*     doesn't do anything if we're already using our standard palette.*   In 320 mode now we use a color table with the same colors as the*     standard 640-mode colors.** 30-Mar-91 DAL (2.0d7)*   Now we draw the boot icons by calling ShowBootInfo (Misc Tools).** 1-Apr-91 DAL (2.0d8)*   Took out X coordinate fudging for drawing an icon in the list;*     they were drawing too far to the right.  Just force it even*     instead.*   We now validate the CDev.Data.2.0 header fields.*   New routine ClosingCDevWindow cleans up while we're closing.*   Added new field owbCDevItemPtr to the window block structure.*   Ack!  Twilight was not preserving the current resource file*     when I gave it an EventsCDEV message.  Fixed so that it doesn't*     matter.*   Now sets current resource file when handling an Action or Close.*   Double-clicking a CDev that is already open just brings it to the*     front.*   Help button is enabled only if exactly one icon is selected.*   Changed data file name to "CDev.Data" (not "CDev.Data.2.0").*   CDev.Data file is now created as invisible.** === released on 6.0d30 ===** 7-Apr-91 DAL (2.0d9)*   Change hotkey from Apple-ESC to Apple-Shift-ESC to avoid conflicting*     with the Installer and Platinum Paint.*   Added WaitCursor and InitCursor in doAboutBox, InitCursor on open.*   Finished code to zoom CDevs closed and mark their icons closed.** === released on 6.0d31 ===** 16-Apr-91 DAL (2.0d10)*   Fix opening/closing of CDevs so that if the CDev puts up a modal*     dialog of some sort, which calls GetNextEvent, that it doesn't*     get really confused if another CDev was already open and gets*     to process its activate or deactivate event during that time.** === released on 6.0d32 ===** 17-Apr-91 DAL (2.0d11)*   Invalid signature word on data file was being propogated to new file.*   Disk full on writing data file was not forcing file to be destroyed.** === released on 6.0d33 and 34 ===** 30-Apr-91 DAL (2.0d12)*   Show watch cursor on CDev help but not CP help.  Was backwards.*   Fix double-clicking in the air so it doesn't blink the OK button.** === missed 6.0d35 by 30 seconds ===** 13-May-91 DAL (2.0d13)*   Made the data file get created Visible again, since sometimes it's*   convenient to throw it out manually.*   Removed some dead cursor-preservation stuff from NDAOpen.*   Added Option key check at NDAOpen for opening Finder window.** 14-May-91 DAL*   Fixed NDAInit so it doesn't crash if you boot under pre-6.0.** 3-Jun-91 DAL (2.0d14)*   Fixed modifiers on Help button key equivalents.*   Added error check on boot-time init of a CDev.  Doesn't crash*     if the resource can't be loaded.  Instead, it X-es out the*     icon and calls SysBeep2($000C).** 11-Jun-91 DAL (still 2.0d14)*   Now passes CDev window pointer to the EventsCDEV message (data2).*   This didn't used to be documented to the world, but now it is,*     and AppleShare was depending on it.** 13-Jun-91 DAL (2.0d15)*   You can double-click on an -inactive- CDev now.  (Why not?)** 24-Jun-91 DAL (2.0d16)*   Now we grab a copy of the rWindColor(07ff0001) for a CDev window,*     instead of hard-coding a lined color table.*   Made the About... button invisible.*   Clicking on the version is the same as clicking on About.** 25-Jun-91 DAL (2.0d17)*   BootCDEV now passes buffer pointer in data1.  Setting bit 0 of*     the first word of the buffer makes the CP X out the CDev icon.** 8-Jul-91 DAL (to be 2.0d19 on 6.0d43)*   No longer trashes memory when closing an "orphaned" Control Panel.** 10-Jul-91 DAL (still 2.0d19)*   Fixed tellFinderOpenWindow buffer (was too short).*   Accepts request $9001 to open the main Control Panels window.** 11-Jul-91 DAL (still 2.0d19)*   No longer accesses SCBs directly!  (For CloseView compatibility.)*   Now forces a valid port around CtlNewRes call (for Prizm compatibilty).*   Edit actions are now passed along to CDevs if wantEdit bit is set.** 23-Jul-91 DAL (2.0d20)*   Better handling of long Control Panel names when drawing icons.  If*   name won't fit, we draw with SetCharExtra(-1).  If it still won't fit,*   we let it stick off the ends.** 20-Aug-91 DAL (2.0d21 on 6.0d46+)*   Always use the correct CDev Flags word when deciding to call*   MachineCDEV!  (Problem made evident by AppleShare CDev 2.0, which*   has WantMachine set.)  Added missing "jsr UpdateFlagsBuffer".** 3-Sep-91 DAL (2.0d22 on 6.0d47)*   Now handles MachineCDEV returning 0--previously did not bother*     to close the unwanted CDev's resource fork or check if we should*     shut down the Resource Manager.*   Does not display an error (like $0120) after MachineCDEV returns 0.*   MainContentDraw and CDevContentDraw now set the CurResourceFile*     around DrawControls.*   Translates Command-Z/X/C/V into SystemEdit, if wantEdit is set.*   Main window position is saved in a rTwoRects(1) resource (first*     rect is 320, second is 640).*   Accepts finderSaysOpenFailed if MachineCDEV failed.** 9-Sep-91 DAL (2.0d23)*   Made option-open or option-double-click close the main window after*     opening a control panel.  (The Close is scheduled to happen later*     at a safe time.)** 15-Sep-91 DAL (2.0d24)*   Opening the main CP window now grabs resources from the correct*     resource file, never from CDevs' resource files by accident.** 16-Sep-91 DAL (2.0d24 for 6.0d49)*   Saves window positions of individual Control Panels, using named*     rTwoRect resources in the $0077xxxx range in the main control*     panels file.  First rect is 320, second is 640.  Only the top-*     left point of each rectangle is used.** 17-Sep-91 DAL*   Make CDev.Data invisible again.** 29-Sep-91 DAL*   The RunQueue task was not calling Push/PopGlobalStuff--was causing*     problems when a CDev displayed an alert during MachineCDEV or*     OpenCDEV, etc.*   Was not preserving the old SCBs correctly when activating one of*     my windows (added plx phx in loop).** 2-Oct-91 DAL (2.0d26)*   Load and start QD Aux if necessary.** 13-Oct-91 DAL (2.0d27)*   Force an Update event right after opening a control panel.*   Ackeret wants Command-O to work like Return for the Open button...okay.** 14-Oct-91 DAL*   Changed handleMenuKey mask from $1B00 to $1300 so that Option-Command-*     Shift-Esc will work (opens the CDevs folder).** 25-Oct-91 DAL (2.0d28 for 6.0d55)*   Added an InvalZoomRect call on open so it redraws as grayed-out even if*     the CDev puts up an AlertWindow during open.** 28-Oct-91 DAL (still 2.0d28)*   Command-? now works for credits as advertised (like clicking on the*     version number).** 29-Oct-91 DAL*   Moved the rIcon "X" resource to Sys.Resources.** 30-Oct-91 DAL (2.0d29 for 6.0d56)*   Run-event handler now preserves and sets the CurResourceApp and*   CurResourceFile.** 11-Oct-91 DAL (2.0d30 for 6.0d57).*   When opening the main window, we make it update right away to avoid*   ugly partly-drawn window if you start typing before it draws.** 19-Nov-91 DAL (2.0d31 for 6.0d59)*   Fixed Run events to work for all windows.** 3-Dec-91 DAL (2.0d32 for 6.0d60)*   When opening a resource file, we now always set the system preferences*     to prompt for the disk, and to *not* allow a Cancel button.** 4-Dec-91 DAL (still for d60)*   Force main window updates on CDev open/close, since they could scroll the*     list before a natural update gets processed.*   Added a missing +2 in the Run event handling from 19-Nov.** 9-Dec-91 DAL (2.0d33 for 6.0d61)*   Added check to avoid doing a Close(0) if we try to read CDev.Data but*     it does not exist.** 10-Dec-91 DAL (still for d61)*   Command-? is now Help, just like Command-H.  (Human Interface guidelines*     say Command-? is not for About.)** 27-Jan-92 DAL (for 6.0d66)*   Around the call to ToBramSetup, we no longer force the bank register to*     $00.  The firmware now does this (Tool.Setup/Misc.Tools).** 5..6-Feb-92 DAL (for 6.0d70)*   Turned off debug symbols (there was only one).*   Since SetPfx was not disposing of the handle passed to it, each time you*     opened and closed the main window, you orphaned a pair of handles*     (which stored the old values of prefixes 0 and 8).*   Optimizations (pCount is always 2 in getPfx and SetPfx; changed a few*     and #$7fff to ASL A, LSR A).*   Cleaned up some old comments.*   Fixed copyright date in the Credits window (click on version number).*   No longer responds to Printing a CDev from the Finder (only Open*     works now); we weren't checking the printFlag in finderSaysBeforeOpen.*   Now keeps the CDev pathname in the window refcon structure.*   Keeps the CDevItemsHandle, CDevPathsHandle, and CDevIconsHandle data*     around when *any* of our windows are open, not just the main window.*   Fixed several bugs where things were confused if you opened CDevs using*     a combination of the main window and the Finder.** 7-Feb-92 DAL (for 6.0d70)*   When showing a CDev's Help window, we need to provide Text Edit and*     Font Manager, so that the Help routine does not try to start them*     up (some do, and they get left started because the CDev never has*     a chance to close them, if the CDev itself is not open).*   Fixed a QDAuxStartUp which was supposed to be a QDAuxStatus.  No actual*     effect, since QD Aux is already available (Window Mgr starts it up),*     redundant QDAuxStartUp calls have no effect, and QDAuxStartUp was*     not changing the $0000 result space from the intended status call.*   Added missing STA/Y ZoomRectPtr, so that zooming down to a closing*     CDev icon always remembers to invalidate the icon in the main window.*   Fixed bone-head design error from yesterday--it makes no sense to try*     calling RebuildTheMemRec (I can't preserve fields, because the thing*     gets built out of order and then sorted).  Now I use FindListIndex to*     find things when I need to mark them open.********************************************************************************** Version 2.1 for System 6.0.1** 16-Mar-92 DAL, v2.1d1 (for 6.1d2)*   When overwriting an existing CDev.Data file, make sure to unlock*     it first!  The old Control Panel created the file with no Write*     access, so we were failing to overwrite it (added one SetFileInfoGS).*   When trying to open CDev.Data for writing, if we got an error we were*     doing a Close with a stale reference number.  Fixed.** 2-Jul-92 DAL (2.1d6 on 6.0.1d6)*   Action routine accepts reOpenAction ($000C) by calling the Open routine*     to let it decide whether to do a SelectWindow or a tellFinderOpenWindow.** 15-Jul-92 DAL (2.1d7 for 6.0.1d7)*   Use new calls OpenResourceFileByID and InvalOneCtlByID.*   Added SpecialEventHandling so Command-Ctrl-Esc works when my windows*     are in front (with and without Option).** 29-Jul-92 DAL (2.1d9 for 6.0.1d9)*   Changed cpOpenCDev handler so the finderSaysBeforeOpen handler handles*     it (only difference is a smaller pcount is allowed).** 3-Sep-92 DAL (2.0d10 for 6.0.1d10)*   Created new internalOpenCDev request handler to work how cpOpenCDev*     used to work.  Fixed bug introduced in d9 where opening a control*     panel did not correctly mark it open & gray the icon, so you had*     problems getting Help on it or opening it again (which should just*     bring it to the front).** 28-Oct-92 DAL (2.0d12 for 6.0.1d12)*   On closing a control panel, call cbp to update daylight savings time*     stuff.** 2-Nov-92 DAL (still d12)*   When calling FixMenuBar, sets System menu bar.** 23-Nov-92 DAL (d12)*   When calling HiliteMenu to hilite or unhilite the Apple menu, passes*     flag values of $8001 and $8000 instead of 1 and 0.  This makes the*     hiliting work right even for a text-based Apple character with a*     weird color table.** 3-Mar-93 SS (for 6.0.1d14)*   Added WhooshRect to the main window opening and closing.** 16-Mar-93 SS (for 6.0.1d15)*   Fixed a random memory trashing bug when there are no active CDEVs.*   Removed QDAux load/startup code as not needed.** 16-Mar-93 DAL (6.0.1d15)*   Yanked out the muck-with-color-tables code and put it into QD Aux,*   as UseColorTable and RestoreColorTable.**   Get rid of the extra color table swapping that happens when switching*   between two windows that both need my color table.  See nasty-looking*   routines DeactivateIfNotMyWindowNext and IgnoreOneDeactivate.** 22-Apr-93 DAL (6.0.1d17)*   Change coypright to include 1993.** 6-May-93 DAL (still 6.0.1d17)*   Removed a couple of JSL UseStandardColorTable calls.********************************************************************************;; VARIOUS NOTES for the future;; Criteria for accepting a finderSaysOpenFailed is not ideal.  Should; always accept based on filetype, display some kind of failure message?;; avoid palette flicker when switching between different CP windows;;; Limitations to remove;; Data file path is local and hard-coded (*:System:CDevs:CDev.Data);; NOTE: Some CDevs (like AppleShare 1.x) expect the CP to dispose of some memory;       for them.  This could be tricky, since I have a lot of CDevs sharing the;       same memory IDs right now, or at least sharing the same Res Mgr ID.;       But I can allocate a separate ID and use SetHandleID when I load their;       rCDEVCode resource.  Then they will call MMStartUp and allocate memory;       with that ID.  I can either allocate new handles, or limit it to 15 open;       Control Panels & use the aux IDs.;; --------------; Options dialog; --------------; "Geek options" dialog, set key equivalent?; Set the initially-selected CDev (record by name); Set the key equivalent & modifiers to open up Control Panels (at MenuKey time);; ------; issues; ------; reduce memory fragmentation; Make sure resources are always released appropriately; Make the error handling bulletproof; The "owbCDevNum" field seems to have turned out to be useless.  Oops, take it out.;; --------------------; UNRESOLVED QUESTIONS; --------------------; Need a wantCursor flag bit?  How should this work?; How can CDevs cleanly use extra tools?; Can a CDev close itself cleanly?; How can a CDev specify that it requires Control Panel 2.0? (can't; 1.0 doesn't check); Should CDevs be allowed to specify features of their window frame?;   Grow/zoom/scroll bars/grow box.;; Control Panel memory use--need some dynamic segments/etc.********************************************************************************* In Control Panel 2.0, CDevs are opened in their own separate windows.  You* can have more than one CDev open at a time, and they have more space available* because they don't have to share with the CDev list.** What goes away?** CDev.Init goes away, because CP 2.0 does that work at DeskShutDown time (the* system calls DeskShutDown at boot time, before launching the application).** The old and BIG CDev.Data file goes away, and it's replaced by a smaller* version.** How it works:** ...** The CP keeps the Resource Manager started up with the CP's memory ID whenever* the main window *or* any CDev windows are open.** Whenever the Main window is open, the CP has data structures about all the* CDevs in the *:System:CDevs folder.** NumCDevsOpen is the number of CDev windows open.  MainWindPtr is non-NIL when* the main window is open.***************************************************************************************************************************************************************DebugSymbols	equ 0	include 'all.macros'	include 'e16.event'	include 'e16.window'	include 'e16.resources'ExpandPathLength	equ 300	;6-Feb-92 DAL********************************************************************************* Constants for main window********************************************************************************TheListWidth	equ 95	;max width for icon name********************************************************************************* Vectors********************************************************************************ToBRAMSetup	equ $e10094********************************************************************************* Filetype equates********************************************************************************CDevFileType	equ $00C7CDevDataFileType	equ $00F9********************************************************************************* System Version numbers********************************************************************************MinQDVersion	equ $0307	;minimum QD version required (6.0)********************************************************************************* rCDevFlags equates********************************************************************************CanMakeInactive	equ $8000	;CP 2.0 does not use thisupdateSSFromBRAM	equ $4000	;call ToBRAMSetup after every HitCDEVwantAvailable1	equ $2000	;future expansionwantAvailable2	equ $1000	;future expansionwantEdit	equ $0800	;CDev wants Edit codes (Undo..Clear)wantRun	equ $0400wantHit	equ $0200wantRect	equ $0100wantAbout	equ $0080wantCreate	equ $0040wantEvents	equ $0020wantClose	equ $0010wantInit	equ $0008wantShutDown	equ $0004wantBoot	equ $0002wantMachine	equ $0001********************************************************************************* CDev message codes********************************************************************************MachineCDEV	equ 1BootCDEV	equ 2	;called at boot, no parametersShutDownCDEV	equ 3	;not usedInitCDEV	equ 4	;call after CreateCDEV (init controls)CloseCDEV	equ 5	;dispose of extra stuffEventsCDEV	equ 6	;give data1=event record before TaskMasterDACreateCDEV	equ 7	;create controls, window=data1AboutCDEV	equ 8	;data1=help window pointerRectCDEV	equ 9	;data1=pointer to rectangle to modifyHitCDEV	equ 10	;data1=control handle, data2=control IDRunCDEV	equ 11	;no parametersEditCDEV	equ 12	;New for 2.0: CDev wants Edit events********************************************************************************* Member Record structure for the List in the main window********************************************************************************oMemName	equ 0oMemFlags	equ 4oMemIcon	equ 6oMemState	equ 10oMemCDevNumber	equ 12oMemItemPtr	equ 14LISTMEMSIZE	equ 18********************************************************************************* The CDev data file on disk is a concatenation of:*   CDevItemList (header + array of CDev items)*   CDevPathsHandle (concatenation of wString pathnames)*   CDevIconsHandle (contcatenation of icons)** These are three separate handles in memory.** CDevList offsets:********************************************************************************oCDevListSignature	equ 0	;must be 'DV' ($5644)oCDevListVersion	equ 2	;must be $0001oCDevListCount	equ 4	;number of CDev items followingCDEVLISTHEADERSIZE	equ 6oCDevListItems	equ 6	;array of CDev items starts here********************************************************************************* CDev Item structure** WARNING: Be sure to update CDevItemTemplate if you change fields here!********************************************************************************oCDevItemSize	equ 0	          ;number of bytes in this structureoCDevItemCreateDate	equ oCDevItemSize+2	          ;CDev file creation dateoCDevItemPathOffset	equ oCDevItemCreateDate+8     ;offset into CDevPathsHandleoCDevItemIconOffset	equ oCDevItemPathOffset+4     ;offset into CDevIconsHandleoCDevItemState	equ oCDevItemIconOffset+4     ;WORD: $0002 = open (like Icon mode) *** NOT USED ***oCDevItemWindow	equ oCDevItemState+2          ;LONG: window pointer to CDev windowoCDevItemFlags	equ oCDevItemWindow+4         ;copy of rCDevFlags resourceoCDevItemEnabled	equ oCDevItemFlags+2oCDevItemVersion	equ oCDevItemEnabled+1oCDevItemMachine	equ oCDevItemVersion+1oCDevItemReserved	equ oCDevItemMachine+1oCDevItemRect	equ oCDevItemReserved+1oCDevItemName	equ oCDevItemRect+8oCDevItemAuthor	equ oCDevItemName+16oCDevItemVerStr	equ oCDevItemAuthor+33CDEVITEMSIZE	equ oCDevItemVerStr+9FLAGSSIZE	equ CDEVITEMSIZE-oCDevItemFlags********************************************************************************* WindBlock structure offsets* (each CDev window's refcon points to one of these)********************************************************************************owbTheCDevItem	equ 0	;first we have a whole CDev Item structureowbResFileNum	equ CDEVITEMSIZEowbRawCDevNumber	equ owbResFileNum+2owbCDevCodePtr	equ owbRawCDevNumber+2owbCDevItemPtr	equ owbCDevCodePtr+4owbWindTitle	equ owbCDevItemPtr+4owbCDevPath	equ owbWindTitle+20	;class-1 string* CDEV PATH MUST BE LAST!  It has a variable size.**************************************************************************************************************************************************************** Main Window control IDs********************************************************************************ListControlID	equ 1	;the listOpenControlID	equ 2	;"Open" buttonCDevHelpControlID	equ 3	;"Help" buttonCPHelpControlID	equ 4	;"About" buttonVersionControlID	equ 5	;the CP version (stat text)********************************************************************************* SendRequest codes that we accept********************************************************************************internalOpenCDev	equ $9900	;3-Sep-92 DAL for 6.0.1d10cpOpenCDev	equ $9000cpOpenControlPanels	equ $9001finderSaysHello	equ $0100finderSaysGoodbye	equ $0101finderSaysBeforeOpen equ $0104finderSaysOpenFailed equ $0105systemSaysMenuKey	equ $0f01tellFinderOpenWindow equ $8002********************************************************************************* Structure of the cpOpenCDev / finderSaysBeforeOpen parm block********************************************************************************opCount	equ 0oPathname	equ opCount+2oSmallRect	equ oPathname+4oFiletype	equ oSmallRect+4oAuxtype	equ oFiletype+2oFinderModifiers	equ oAuxtype+4oFinderIconHandle	equ oFinderModifiers+2oPrintFlag	equ oFinderIconHandle+4**************************************************************************************************************************************************************** NDA header********************************************************************************CtlPanelNDA	proc export	dc.l NDAOpen	; Pointer to the open routine	dc.l NDAClose	; Pointer to the close routine	dc.l NDAAction	; Pointer to the action routine glue	dc.l NDAInit	; Pointer to the init routine glueNDAPeriod	dc.w $FFFF	; How often the NDA gets NDAEventMask	dc.w $A16E	; Describes what events the NDA wants	dc.b '**'	; two place-holding charactersNDAMenuLine	dc.b 'Control Panels'	dc.b '\H'myMenuID	dc.b '**'	; \H and two place-holding characters	dc.b 0	; The menu item string terminator*******************************************************************************MyMemID	dc.w 0	export MainWindPtrMainWindPtr	dc.l 0	export MainResFileMainResFile	dc.w 0	;this is 0 if our resource fork isn't openNumCDevsOpen	dc.w 0	;number of CDev windows open*******************************************************************************	import HandleActivate	import WhatAccessRequest********************************************************************************* GetMyMainMenuID** Output: A = my NDA menu item's ID, to pass to OpenNDA to open me********************************************************************************	export GetMyMainMenuIDGetMyMainMenuID	lda >myMenuID	rtl********************************************************************************* AdjustNumCDevsOpen** Input: -1, 0, or 1 in A to decrement, retrieve, or increment the number*        of CDev windows open** Output: A = new number of CDev windows open********************************************************************************	export AdjustNumCDevsOpenAdjustNumCDevsOpen	clc	adc >NumCDevsOpen	sta >NumCDevsOpen	rtl********************************************************************************* NDAInit** A=0  for shutdown* A<>0 for startup********************************************************************************	import cbpNDAInit	phb	phk	plb	pha	;save code on stack	jsr CheckMinQDVersion	pla	;added 14-May-91 DAL	bcc @exit	pha	;added 14-May-91 DAL	pha	_MMStartUp	pla	ora #$0100	sta MyMemID* Adjust for daylight savings time!	jsl cbp	;check BRAM parameters (Stein's code)	pla	bne @startup	jsr ndaInitShutdown	bra @exit@startup	jsr ndaInitStartup@exit	plb	rtl********************************************************************************* ndaInitStartup -- our Init routine got called with A<>0********************************************************************************ndaInitStartup	jsr InstallRequestProc	rts********************************************************************************* ndaInitShutDown--our Init routine got called with A=0** Do CDev.Init tasks here--we need to call the BootCDEV routine* of every CDev that wants it.********************************************************************************ndaInitShutdown	jsr RemoveRequestProc	lda bootedFlag	bne @booted	jsr DoWantBoot	sec	ror bootedFlag@booted	rtsbootedFlag	dc.w 0	;nonzero if we already did boot messages********************************************************************************* DoWantBoot** Send the BootCDEV message to every CDev that has its wantBoot flag bit set.********************************************************************************DoWantBoot	jsl StartResourceManager	jsl GetCDevList	phd	pea 0	;index = 0..CDevListCount-1	pushlong CDevItemsHandle	pha	pha	;space for path pointer	tsc	tcd@pathptr	equ 1@itemPtr	equ @pathptr+4@counter	equ @itemPtr+4	ldy #2	lda [@itemPtr],y	tax	lda [@itemPtr]	sta @itemPtr	stx @itemPtr+2	;dereffed CDevItemsHandle into pointer@walk	lda @counter	cmp CDevListCount	bcs @done	ldy #oCDevItemFlags	lda [@itemPtr],y	and #wantBoot	beq @skipThis	jsr @BootThisCDev@skipThis	clc	lda @itemPtr	adc #CDEVITEMSIZE	sta @itemPtr	bcc @1	inc @itemPtr+2@1	inc @counter	bra @walk@done	pla	pla	;pulled pathname pointer	pla	pla	;pulled CDev item pointer	pla	;pulled counter	pld	jsl DisposeCDevList	jsl StopResourceManager	rts********************************************************************************* @BootThisCDev** @itemPtr points to the CDev's item record* @pathPtr is available for us to use** We need to draw the CDev's icon on the boot screen,* open its resource fork, load its code, and then* call the boot message.** Output: none********************************************************************************@BootThisCDev*** draw the boot-time icon	ldy #oCDevItemIconOffset+2	lda [@itemPtr],y	pha	dey	dey	lda [@itemPtr],y	pha	phd	pushlong CDevIconsHandle	tsc	tcd	ldy #2	lda [1],y	tax	lda [1]	clc	adc 7,s	sta 1	txa	adc 7+2,s	sta 3	pla	plx	pld	;icon pointer in XA	ply	ply	;throw away icon offset	pea 0	pea 0	;no string for ShowBootInfo	phx	pha		_ShowBootInfo*** done drawing icon	lda CDevPathsHandle+2	ldy CDevPathsHandle	sta @pathPtr+2	sty @pathPtr	ldy #2	lda [@pathPtr],y	tax	lda [@pathPtr]	sta @pathPtr	stx @pathPtr+2	ldy #oCDevItemPathOffset	clc	lda @pathPtr	adc [@itemPtr],y	sta @pathPtr	lda @pathPtr+2	iny	iny	adc [@itemPtr],y	sta @pathPtr+2	pha	;space for OpenResourceFile result	pea 1	;access = read-only	pea 0	pea 0	;map address	pei <@pathPtr+2	pei <@pathPtr	jsr GetAndFixPrefs	;3-Dec-91 DAL	_OpenResourceFile	jsr RestorePrefs	;3-Dec-91 DAL	plx	bcs @outtahere	phx	;keep for CloseResourceFile	pha	pha	;space for LoadResource	pea rCDevCode	pushlong #1	;ID=1	_LoadResource	plx	pla	bcs @couldNotLoadCode	pha	phx	phd	tsc	tcd	ldy #1	;deref code handle into JSL operand	lda [3],y	sta @toTheCDev+2	lda [3]	sta @toTheCDev+1	pld;;;	;pla;;;	;pla	;pull pointer;;;	;pha;;;	;pha	;push CDev result space	pea BootCDEV	pushlong #bootResultBuffer  ;data1 = buffer pointer	stz bootResultBuffer	lda #0	pha	pha	;data2 = reserved@toTheCDev	jsl >$777777	;self-modified	pla	pla	;(ignore CDev result)	lsr bootResultBuffer	bcc @noXout	jsr drawXicon@noXout@closeAndExit	_CloseResourceFile@outtahere	rts*** If we couldn't init the CDev, "X" out its icon@couldNotLoadCode	_CloseResourceFile	jsr drawXicon	pea $000c	;operation failed	_SysBeep2	rts** bootResultBuffer** +000: bit 0 = draw an X through me** Other bytes are reserved for future definition*bootResultBuffer	dc.w 0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0********************************************************************************* drawXicon -- draw our rIcon("X") resource over the previous icon********************************************************************************drawXicon	pha	pha	;space for LoadResource	pea rIcon	pushlong #$07FF0058	;Sys.Resources "X" icon	_LoadResource	pla	plx	bcs @ohDang		phd	;XA = icon handle	phx	pha	tsc	tcd	ldy #4	;offset to attributes	lda [1],y	ora #$8000	sta [1],y	;locked handle	dey	dey	;Y=2 for dereference	lda [1],y	ora #$8000	;set bit 31 of icon pointer (overwrite icon)	tax	lda [1]	;XA now = icon pointer, with bit 31 set	pea 0	pea 0	;no string for ShowBootInfo	phx	pha	;icon pointer (bit 31 set = overwrite)	_ShowBootInfo	ldy #4	;offset to attributes	lda [1],y	asl a	lsr a	sta [1],y	;unlocked handle	ply	ply	pld	pea 2	;purge level	pea rIcon	pushlong #$07FF0058	_ReleaseResource@ohDang	rts********************************************************************************* NDAOpen--returns window pointer on stack********************************************************************************result	equ  5	;RTL address and B on the stack alreadyNDAOpen	phb	phk	plb	lda #0	sta result,s	sta result+2,s	;anticipate no window	jsr CheckMinQDVersion	bcs @systemOK*** Use an old call to beep if the System version is too old!@badSystem	_SysBeep	;don't use SysBeep2, it isn't available!	_SysBeep	brl @outtaHere@systemOK*** Start up the List Manager, we'll need it!	pea 0	_ListStatus	pla	bne @gotListMgr	pea $001C	;List Manager	pea $0303	;version 3.3	_LoadOneTool	bcs @badSystem	_ListStartUp@gotListMgr*** removed, QDAux is loaded/started by WindStartup. 16-Mar-93 SS;*** Start up QD Aux, we'll need it!;	pea 0;;;;	_QDAuxStartUp;*** fixed 7-Feb-92 DAL -- typo!;	_QDAuxStatus;*** end 7-Feb-92;	pla;	bne @gotQDAux;;	pea $0012	;QDAux;	pea $0304	;version 3.4;	_LoadOneTool;	bcs @badSystem;	_QDAuxStartUp;@gotQDAux** If the Option key is down, try to open the *:System:CDevs folder* instead of opening the NDA window*	lda >$e0c025	and #$0040	;check option key	beq @dontTryFinder	jsr TryFinderWindow	bcs @dontTryFinder	brl @outtaHere@dontTryFinder	pha	pha	_GetPort	pla	sta oldPort	pla	sta oldPort+2	_WaitCursor	pha	_GetCurResourceApp	pla	sta oldResApp	bcs @error	;possible if Resource Mgr not here!	jsl StartResourceManager	bcs @error	jsr MakeMainWindow	bcs @error	stx MainWindPtr+2	sta MainWindPtr	jsr MakeVersionNumber	jsr PushMainWindPtr	_SetSysWindow	jsr PushMainWindPtr	_SetPort	jsl GetCDevList	jsr FixUpListControl	lda MainWindPtr+2	sta result+2,s	lda MainWindPtr	sta result,s	jsr WhooshOpen	;*** 3-Mar-93 SS		jsr PushMainWindPtr	_ShowWindow*** force main window to update right away	jsr PushMainWindPtr	_BeginUpdate	jsl MainContentDraw	jsr PushMainWindPtr	_EndUpdate@error	lda oldResApp	pha	_SetCurResourceApp	;restore ResourceApp	pushlong oldPort	_SetPort	_InitCursor@outtaHere	plb	rtloldResApp	dc.w 0oldPort	dc.l 0********************************************************************************* TryFinderWindow -- if the Finder is around, let it open up* *:System:CDevs for us********************************************************************************TryFinderWindow	pea tellFinderOpenWindow	pea 1	;by String	pushlong #FinderString	pushlong #thePathname	pushlong #FndrBuff	;output	_SendRequest	rtsFinderString	str 'Apple~Finder~'thePathname	dc.b 14,0,'*:System:CDevs'FndrBuff	dc.w 0	;recvCount (result)	dc.w 0	;finderResult (result)	dc.l 0	;window pointer (result)********************************************************************************* CheckMinQDVersion** Returns SEC if the QuickDraw version is high enough********************************************************************************CheckMinQDVersion	pea 0	_QDVersion	pla	and #$0fff	cmp #MinQDVersion	rts********************************************************************************* MakeVersionNumber** Set the text for the VersionControl (static text), by loading our* rVersion(1) resource and calling VersionString.********************************************************************************MakeVersionNumber	lda MainResFile	jsr UseOnlyThisFile	pha	phx	jsr @MakeVerNum	plx	pla	jsr RestoreOldFile	rts@MakeVerNum	pha	pha	pea $8029	;rVersion	pushlong #1	_LoadResource	bcs @ouch	phd	tsc	tcd	ldy #4	lda [3],y	ora #$8000	sta [3],y	;lock the handle	dey	dey	lda [3],y	;dereference it	tax	lda [3]	sta 3	stx 5	pea 0	;flags for VersionString	lda [3],y	;Y is still 2 from above	pha	lda [3]	pha	;version number to convert	pushlong #versionBuffer	_VersionString	pld	pla	pla	;throw out pointer	pea $ffff	;dispose flag	pea $8029	;rVersion	pushlong #1	_ReleaseResource	pushlong #versionBuffer+1	jsr PushVersionHandle	_SetCtlTitle	lda versionBuffer	and #$00ff	pha	jsr PushVersionHandle	_SetCtlValue	;value is the length of the text	rts@ouch	pla	pla	rtsversionBuffer	ds.b 10PushVersionHandle	lda #VersionControlID	brl PushCtlHandle********************************************************************************* StartResourceManager** If we don't already have the Resource Manager started, then:*   Start up the resource manager*   Log in the CodeResConverter for rCDEVCode*   Open the NDA's resource fork with as-allowed permissions** Returns CLC if successful.********************************************************************************	export StartResourceManagerStartResourceManager	clc	lda MainResfile	bne @done;	pha;	_MMStartUp;	_ResourceStartUp;;*** Log in the CodeResConverter for rCDEVCode;	pha;	pha;	_GetCodeResConverter;	pea rCDEVCode;	pea 1	;log in as Application converter;	_ResourceConverter;;* for OpenResourceFile, push requested access, map handle (0), and pathname;	pha	;space for OpenResourceFile result;;	jsl WhatAccessRequest ;read-only for AppleShare!;	pha;;	lda #0;	pha;	pha	;pushed 0 for resource map;	jsr GetMyPathname;	phy;	pha;	jsr GetAndFixPrefs;	_OpenResourceFile;	jsr RestorePrefs	;preserves Carry from OpenResourceFile;	plx;	bcs @error;	stx MainResFile;@error;@done	rtl*** 15-Jul-92 DAL -- use OpenResourceFileByID, mainly to exercise it	pha	;space for OpenResourceFileByID	jsl WhatAccessRequest ;read-only for AppleShare	pha	;reqAccess for OpenResourceFileByID	pha	;space for MMStartUp	_MMStartUp	;pass ID to OpenResourceFileByID	jsr GetAndFixPrefs	ldx #$2E1E	jsl $e10000;	_OpenResourceFileByID	jsr RestorePrefs	;preserves Carry from OpenResourceFile	pla	;discard result	bcs @done*** Log in the CodeResConverter for rCDEVCode	pha	pha	_GetCodeResConverter	pea rCDEVCode	pea 1	;log in as Application converter	_ResourceConverter	pha	_GetCurResourceFile	pla	sta MainResFile*** end 15-Jul-92@done	rtl********************************************************************************* StopResourceManager** If there are no CDev windows open and the main window isn't open either,* shut down the resource manager.********************************************************************************	export StopResourceManagerStopResourceManager	phb	phk	plb	ldx MainResFile	beq @dontStop	;we don't seem to have started it!	lda NumCDevsOpen	bne @dontStop	lda MainWindPtr+1	bne @dontStop	lda MainResFile	ora #$8000	;force it closed!	pha	_CloseResourceFile	stz MainResFile	_ResourceShutDown@dontStop	plb	rtl********************************************************************************* UseOnlyThisFile** Input:  Resource file number in A** Output:  Current resource file is set, depth is 1*          Previous file in A, previous depth in X********************************************************************************UseOnlyThisFile	pha	pha	;space for cur resource file	_GetCurResourceFile	pha	;space for old depth	pea 1	_SetResourceFileDepth	lda 5,s	;retrieve input	pha	_SetCurResourceFile	plx	;get old depth	pla	;get old file	ply	;throw away copy of input	rts********************************************************************************* RestoreOldFile** Input:  Resource file in A, depth in X********************************************************************************RestoreOldFile	pha	;resource file number	phx	;space for old depth	phx	;new depth	_SetResourceFileDepth	plx	;throw away	_SetCurResourceFile	rts;;; Not needed with OpenResourceFileByID;*******************************************************************************;*;* GetMyPathname;*;* Input: none;*;* Output: pointer to class-one pathname in YA;*;*******************************************************************************;GetMyPathname	pha;	pha	;space for LGetPathname2;	pha	;space for MMStartUp;	_MMStartUp;	pea 1	;file number 1;	_LGetPathname2;	pla;	ply;	rts********************************************************************************* MakeMainWindow--return pointer in XA********************************************************************************MakeMainWindow	import UseStandardPalette*** Removed 6-May-93 DAL;;;	jsl UseStandardPalette	;22-Mar-91 DAL	pha		;15-Sep-91 DAL	_GetCurResourceFile		;	lda MainResFile		;	pha		;	_SetCurResourceFile		;	jsr SetUpMainWindowLocation	;4-Sep-91 DAL	pha	pha	pushlong #0	;title	pushlong #0	;refcon	pushlong #MainContentDraw	pushlong #0	;custom defproc	pea 2	;by Resource	pushlong #1	;resource ID	pea rWindParam1		_NewWindow2	lda 5,s	pha	_SetCurResourceFile	pla	plx	;XA = window pointer	ply	;discard old Resource File setting	rts********************************************************************************* SetUpMainWindowLocation** From rTwoRects(1), get the 320 or 640 rectangle and cram it into the* rWindParam(1) resource.********************************************************************************SetUpMainWindowLocation	pha	pha	pea rTwoRects	pushlong #1	_LoadResource	plx	ply	bcc @noDang	brl @dang@noDang	phy	phx	;re-push rTwoRects(1) handle	phd	tsc	tcd	ldy #4	lda [<3],y	ora #$8000	sta [<3],y	;locked rTwoRects	dey	dey	lda [<3],y	tax	lda [<3]	sta <3	stx <5	;derefed rTwoRects	jsr Bump3by8for640	pei <5	pei <3	;push source pointer for BlockMove	pha	pha	pea rWindParam1	pushlong #1	_LoadResource	phd	tsc	tcd	ldy #2	clc	lda [3]	adc #$3e	;offset to wPosition	tax	lda [3],y	adc #0	sta <5	stx <3	pld	;left dest pointer for BlockMove		pushlong #8	;size of a rect	_BlockMove	;move into rWindParam1 template	pld	plx	plx	;discard long	pha	pha	pea rTwoRects	pushlong #1	_LoadResource	_HUnlock@dang	rtsBump3by8for640	pha	_GetMasterSCB	pla	and #$0080	beq @ok	lda #8	;offset to 640 rectangle	clc	adc <3	sta <3	bcc @ok	inc <5@ok	rts********************************************************************************* RecordMainWindPosition -- if window moved, write its new position to the*                           rTwoRects(1) resource********************************************************************************RecordMainWindPosition; check if resource fork is writeable??	pha	pha	pea rTwoRects	pushlong #1	_LoadResource	plx	ply	bcc @noDang	brl @dang@noDang	phy	phx	phd	tsc	tcd	ldy #4	lda [<3],y	ora #$8000	sta [<3],y	;locked rTwoRects	dey	dey	lda [<3],y	tax	lda [<3]	sta <3	stx <5	;derefed rTwoRects	jsr Bump3by8for640	pha	pha	_GetPort	jsr PushMainWindPtr	_SetPort	stz theWindPos	stz theWindPos+2	pushlong #theWindPos	_LocalToGlobal	_SetPort	lda theWindPos	cmp [3]	bne @dirty	lda theWindPos+2	ldy #2	cmp [3],y	beq @notDirty@dirty	pei 5	pei 3	ldy #2	lda [3],y	eor #$ffff	inc a	;-left	pha	lda [3]	;-top	eor #$ffff	inc a	pha	_OffsetRect	pei 5	pei 3	lda theWindPos+2	pha	lda theWindPos	pha	_OffsetRect	pea $ffff	;true	pea rTwoRects	pushlong #1	_MarkResourceChange@notDirty	pld	plx	plx	;discard long@dang	rtstheWindPos	dc.w 0,0********************************************************************************* FixUpListControl** Inputs:*   CDevListCount -- number of CDevs*   CDevItemsHandle*   CDevPathsHandle*   CDevIconsHandle** Outputs:*   The main window's list control is up to date********************************************************************************FixUpListControl	lda CDevListCount	;make sure there are some! *** 16-Mar-93 SS	bne @some	stz ListMemHandle	;otherwise, obliterate the handle,	stz ListMemHandle+2 ; skip the devastating SelectMember2,	brl @none	; and just dim the buttons.	@some	pha	pha	;space for NewHandle result	pha	pha	;space for Multiply result	pea LISTMEMSIZE	pha	;(CDevListCount)	_Multiply	;leave result on stack for NewHandle	jsr PushDataID		pea $C000	;locked and fixed	pha	pha	;location (ignored)	_NewHandle	pla	sta ListMemHandle	pla	sta ListMemHandle+2;;;	lda #0	;a=0 to build list for the first time (7-Feb-92 DAL);;;	jsr CallBuildMemRec	pushlong ListMemHandle	pushlong CDevItemsHandle	pushlong CDevIconsHandle	pushlong CDevPathsHandle	jsr BuildTheMemRec	pushlong #MainListDraw	pea 1	;start	pushlong ListMemHandle	pea 1	;ListMemHandle is a handle	lda CDevListCount	pha	jsr PushListControl	_NewList2	pushlong #1	;case-insensitive	jsr PushListControl	_SortList2	pea 1	jsr PushListControl	_SelectMember2@none	jsr SetButtonStates	rts;	export RebuildMemRec;RebuildMemRec	lda #$ffff	;A=$FFFF to rebuilt list (preserve selection) (7-Feb-92 DAL);	jsr CallBuildMemRec;	pushlong #1	;case-insensitive;	jsr PushListControl;	_SortList2;	jsr SetButtonStates;	rts;CallBuildMemRec;;;;	tax	;save build/rebuild flag;	pushlong ListMemHandle;	pushlong CDevItemsHandle;	pushlong CDevIconsHandle;	pushlong CDevPathsHandle;;;;	txa	;build/rebuild flag;	jsr BuildTheMemRec;	rts********************************************************************************* PushListControl -- push the handle to the main window's list control********************************************************************************PushListControl	lda #ListControlID	brl PushCtlHandle********************************************************************************* BuildTheMemRec** Stack Inputs:*   HANDLE  ListMemHandle*   HANDLE  CDevItemsHandle*   HANDLE  CDevIconsHandle*   HANDLE  CDevPathsHandle** Other inputs:*   CDevListCount** Outputs:*   The member record handle is done!  It contains pointers into the other*   handles, which had better be locked at this point.********************************************************************************BuildTheMemRec	phd	tsc	tcd@oldD	equ 1@rts	equ @oldD+2@paths	equ @rts+2@icons	equ @paths+4@items	equ @icons+4@memrec	equ @items+4	ldy #2	lda [@paths],y	tax	lda [@paths]	sta @paths	stx @paths+2	lda [@icons],y	tax	lda [@icons]	sta @icons	stx @icons+2	lda [@items],y	tax	lda [@items]	sta @items	stx @items+2	lda [@memrec],y	tax	lda [@memrec]	sta @memrec	stx @memrec+2	stz CDevIndex	;count from 0 up, numbering the CDevs	lda CDevListCount	beq @done@next	pha	ldy #oMemName	clc	lda @items	adc #oCDevItemName	sta [@memrec],y	iny	iny	lda @items+2	adc #0	sta [@memrec],y	ldy #oCDevItemIconOffset+2	lda [@items],y	tax	dey	dey	lda [@items],y	clc	adc @icons	ldy #oMemIcon	sta [@memrec],y	txa	adc @icons+2	iny	iny	sta [@memrec],y	ldy #oMemCDevNumber	lda CDevIndex	sta [@memrec],y	lda #0	ldy #oMemFlags	sta [@memrec],y*** added 6-Feb-92 DAL -- If the CDev is known to be open, set the Open flag	ldy #oCDevItemWindow+1	lda [@items],y	beq @storeState	lda #2	;open@storeState*** end 6-Feb-92	ldy #oMemState	sta [@memrec],y*** added 6-Feb-92 DAL -- store the item pointer in the member record	ldy #oMemItemPtr	lda <@items	sta [<@memrec],y	iny	iny	lda <@items+2	sta [<@memrec],y*** end 6-Feb-92	clc	lda @memrec	adc #LISTMEMSIZE	sta @memrec	bcc @1	inc @memrec+2@1	clc	lda @items	adc #CDEVITEMSIZE	sta @items	bcc @2	inc @items+2@2	inc CDevIndex	pla	dec a	bne @next@done	pld	plx	tsc	clc	adc #16	tcs	phx	rtscdevIndex	dc.w 0********************************************************************************* MainListDraw** Stack on entry:** | previous contents |* |-------------------|* |      rectPtr      |  LONG* |-------------------|* |  memberRecordPtr  |  LONG* |-------------------|* |   ListCtlHandle   |  LONG* |-------------------|* |    RTL Address    |  3 BYTES* |-------------------|*                        <-- stack pointer********************************************************************************** Member Record format:**   +000: oMemName       Name pointer (Pascal string)*   +004: oMemFlags      member flags*   +006: oMemIcon       Icon Pointer*   +010: oMemState      State to draw icon in (the Open bit is valid)*   +012  LISTMEMSIZE********************************************************************************MainListDraw	phd	tsc	tcd@oldD	equ 1@RTL	equ @oldD+2@ListCtlHndl	equ @RTL+3@memRecPtr	equ @ListCtlHndl+4@rectPtr	equ @memRecPtr+4@InputSize	equ 12	;number of bytes to strip* Make a copy of the rect so we can fiddle with it	ldy #6	tyx@copyR	lda [<@rectPtr],y	sta >@LocalRect,x	dey	dey	dex	dex	bpl @copyR	lda #^@LocalRect	ldx #@LocalRect	sta <@rectPtr+2	stx <@rectPtr* Erase the rectangle	pei <@rectPtr+2	pei <@rectPtr	_EraseRect* Draw the CDev's icon	ldy #oMemIcon+2	lda [<@memRecPtr],y	pha	dey	dey	lda [<@memRecPtr],y	pha	;pushed icon		jsr @ComputeIconModeWord	phx	;pushed mode	jsr @ComputeIconXCoord	pha	;pushed X coordinate	lda [<@rectPtr]	;top	inc a	inc a	pha	;pushed Y coordinate (rect.top+2)	_DrawIcon	;icon, mode, x, y* Now draw the CDev's name*** Preserve CharExtra	pha	pha	_GetCharExtra	pha	;space for StringWidth result	ldy #oMemName+2	lda [<@memRecPtr],y	pha	lda [<@memRecPtr]	pha	_StringWidth	;width at 1,s*** Of the string is too wide, use SetCharExtra(-1)	lda 1,s	cmp #TheListWidth	bcc @widthOK	pea $ffff	pea 0	_SetCharExtra	ldy #oMemName+2	lda [<@memRecPtr],y	pha	lda [<@memRecPtr]	pha	_StringWidth	;width at 1,s@widthOK	ldy #6	;right	lda [<@rectPtr],y	sec	ldy #2	;left	sbc [<@rectPtr],y	sec	sbc 1,s*** Do a sign-friendly divide-by-2	cmp #$8000	ror a	clc	ldy #2	;left	adc [<@rectPtr],y	sta [<@rectPtr],y	;stored new Left value	pha	;MoveTo(left,bottom-2)	ldy #4	;bottom	lda [<@rectPtr],y	dec a	dec a	pha	;pushed bottom-2	_MoveTo	ldy #oMemName+2	lda [<@memRecPtr],y	pha	lda [<@memRecPtr]	pha	_DrawString	ldy #oMemFlags	lda [<@memRecPtr],y	and #$0080	beq @noInvertName* bottom -= 1; top = bottom-9; left--; right=left+width+1	ldy #4	lda [<@rectPtr],y	dec a	sta [<@rectPtr],y	sec	sbc #9	sta [<@rectPtr]	;store new top (offset 0)	ldy #2	;left	lda [<@rectPtr],y	dec a	sta [<@rectPtr],y	clc	adc 1,s	inc a	ldy #6	;right	sta [<@rectPtr],y	pei <@rectPtr+2	pei <@rectPtr	_InvertRect@noInvertName	pla	;discard StringWidth result	_SetCharExtra	;23-Jul-91 DAL -- restore CharExtra* Remove the 12 bytes of input parameters and return	pld	lda 2,s	sta 2+@InputSize,s	lda 1,s	sta 1+@InputSize,s	tsc	clc	adc #@InputSize	tcs	rtl@LocalRect	ds.b 8********************************************************************************* ComputeIconXCoord** Inputs: @rectPtr and Master SCB** Output: Return value in A********************************************************************************@ComputeIconXCoord	ldy #6	;right	lda [<@rectPtr],y	sec	ldy #2	;left	sbc [<@rectPtr],y	lsr a	sec	sbc #28	clc	ldy #2	;left	adc [<@rectPtr],y	pha** If 320 mode then IconX += 14*	pha	_GetMasterSCB	pla	and #$0080	bne @not320	pla	clc	adc #14	pha@not320		lda 1,s	;just force it even!	and #1	clc	adc 1,s	plx	;discard	rts********************************************************************************* ComputeIconModeWord** Start with the mode word in the member record.  If list member* is selected, turn on the Selected bit.** (Return value in X.)********************************************************************************@ComputeIconModeWord	ldy #oMemState	lda [<@memRecPtr],y	and #$fffe	;ignore the Selected bit	tax	ldy #oMemFlags	lda [<@memRecPtr],y	and #$0080	beq @notSelected	inx	;turn on the Selected bit@notSelected	rts********************************************************************************* MainContentDraw -- Bank register not set!********************************************************************************MainContentDraw	pha	_GetCurResourceFile	lda >MainResFile	pha	_SetCurResourceFile	pha	pha	_GetPort	_DrawControls	_SetCurResourceFile	rtl********************************************************************************* PushMainWindPtr -- put window pointer on stack above RTS address********************************************************************************	export PushMainWindPtrPushMainWindPtr	plx	lda MainWindPtr+2	pha	lda MainWindPtr	pha	phx	rts********************************************************************************* NDAClose -- close the main window********************************************************************************	import DeactivateIfNotMyWindowNextNDAClose	phb	phk	plb	lda MainWindPtr+1	beq @notOpen	pha	_GetCurResourceFile	lda MainResFile	pha	_SetCurResourceFile;	pha;	pha;	_GetPort;	jsr PushMainWindPtr;	_SetPort;; Don't need to do anything here....;	_SetPort	;restore old port	jsr RecordMainWindPosition	jsr PushMainWindPtr	;*** 3-Mar-93 SS	_HideWindow	;*** 3-Mar-93 SS	jsr WhooshClosed	;*** 3-Mar-93 SS		jsr PushMainWindPtr	_CloseWindow	stz MainWindPtr	stz MainWindPtr+2;;;	lda #0;;;	jsl HandleActivate	jsl DeactivateIfNotMyWindowNext	;17-Mar-93 DAL	_SetCurResourceFile	jsl StopResourceManager	jsl DisposeListMemHndl   ;6-Feb-92 DAL	jsl CondDisposeCDevList  ;get rid of it if we're done!@notOpen	plb	rtl******************************************************************* 3-Mar-93 SS** Whoosh Open & Closed** input: none** output: none********************************************************************************WhooshOpen	lda #$8000	bra dirSetWhooshClosed	lda #0dirSet	pha			pea 0	pushlong #smallRect		pha	; setup the bigRect	pha	jsr PushMainWindPtr	_GetStructRgn	phd	tsc	tcd		lda [3]	;deref the handle to the region	tax	ldy #2	lda [3],y	sta 3+2	stx 3		ldy #6+2@loop	lda [3],y	sta bigRect-2,y	dey	dey	bne @loop		pld	pla	pla		pushlong #bigRect	_WhooshRect	rtssmallRect	dc.w 14,14,15,15bigRect	dc.w 00,00,00,00**************************************************************************************************************************************************************** NDAAction for the main window** A=action* YX=pointer********************************************************************************NDAAction	phd	phb	phk	plb	pha	;action = <5	phy	;ptr high = <3	phx	;ptr low = <1	tsc	tcd	pha	_GetCurResourceFile	lda MainResFile	pha	_SetCurResourceFile	pha	pha	_GetPort	;leave old port on stack	jsr PushMainWindPtr	_SetPort	lda <5	asl a	tax	cmp #actionEnd-actionTable	bcs @tooBig	jsr (actionTable,x)@tooBig	_SetPort	;restore old port	_SetCurResourceFile	;added 1-Apr-91 DAL	plx	;pull ptr low	plx	;pull ptr high	plx	;pull action	plb	pld	lda #0	;return value	rtlactionTable	dc.w null	;0 = unused	dc.w doEvent	;1 = eventAction	dc.w doRun	;2 = runAction	dc.w doCursor	;3 = cursorAction	dc.w null	;4 = unused	dc.w doUndo	;5 = undoAction	dc.w doCut	;6 = cutAction	dc.w doCopy	;7 = copyAction	dc.w doPaste	;8 = pasteAction	dc.w doClear	;9 = clearAction*** added 2-Jul-92 DAL	dc.w doSysClick	;10 = sysClickAction	dc.w doOptionalClose ;11 = optionalCloseAction	dc.w doReOpen	;12 = reOpenAction*** end 2-Jul-92actionEnd********************************************************************************* Boring actions received by the Main window********************************************************************************doSysClickdoOptionalClosedoCursordoUndodoCutdoCopydoPastedoClearnull	rts********************************************************************************* doReOpen (new routine 2-Jul-92 DAL)** We are already open, and they chose use again from the Apple menu (or* NDAOpen happened some other way, like thru our key equivalent).** If the Option key is down, do the Finder window thang.  Otherwise* let the system bring us to the front as usual.** If we already took care of everything, stuff a $0001 at [<1] to tell* the system so.********************************************************************************doReOpen	lda >$e0c025	and #$0040	;check option key	beq @normal	jsr TryFinderWindow	bcs @normal	lda #1	sta [<1]@normal	rts********************************************************************************* doRun -- run event received by the main window********************************************************************************doRun	rts********************************************************************************* doEvent -- Event Manager event received by the Main window********************************************************************************	import DeactivateIfNotMyWindowNextdoEvent	jsl SpecialEventHandling	;added 15-Jul-92 DAL	pei 3	pei 1	pushlong #myTaskRec	pushlong #16	_BlockMove*** make Command-O like Return	lda myTaskWhat	cmp #3	;keyDown event	bne @notCommandKey	lda myTaskMods	and #$0100	beq @notCommandKey	lda myTaskMsg*** do Command-? or Command-/	cmp #'?'	beq @isQuestion	cmp #'/'	bne @notQuestion@isQuestion*** blink the Help button & do Help	lda #'H'	sta myTaskMsg	bra @cmdKeyDone@notQuestion	and #$00df	cmp #'O'	;allow "o" or "O"	bne @notCommandO	lda #13	;Return	sta myTaskMsg	bra @cmdKeyDone@notCommandO@notCommandKey@cmdKeyDone	pha	;result space	pha	;input mask (ignored)	pushlong #myTaskRec	_TaskMasterDA	pla	cmp #activateEvt	bne @notActivate	lda myTaskMods*** added 17-Mar-93 DAL	and #1	bne @normal	jsl DeactivateIfNotMyWindowNext	rts@normal*** end 17-Mar-93	jsl HandleActivate	rts@notActivate	cmp #wInControl	bne @notControlHit** Now myTaskData2 = control handle, myTaskData4 = control ID*	lda myTaskData4@hitControlA	asl a	tax	cmp #@ctlTableEnd-@ctlTable	bcs @bogus	jsr (@ctlTable,x)@bogus@notControlHit	rts@ctlTable	dc.w @null	;0	dc.w hitList	;1	dc.w hitOpen	;2	dc.w hitHelp	;3	dc.w hitAbout	;4	dc.w hitVersion	;5@ctlTableEnd@null	rts********************************************************************************* hitOpen -- they want to open all the selected CDevs********************************************************************************hitOpen	pha	pha	_GetCursorAdr	_WaitCursor@loop	pha	;space for ResetMember2 result	jsr PushListControl	_ResetMember2	pla	beq @done	jsr OpenCDevNumberA	bra @loop@done	jsr SetButtonStates	_SetCursor	rts********************************************************************************* OpenCDevNumberA** Input:  A = item number from the main list (1=first)** WARNING: Stack frame shared between OpenCDevNumberA, LocateCDevNumberA,*          DerefAYToPtr, and AboutCDevNumberA********************************************************************************	import globalErrorCode:dataOpenCDevNumberA	phd	pha	pha	;space for pointer	dec a	;make cdev number 0-based	sta TheRawCDevNumber	pha	;raw cdev number	pha	;translated cdev number	tsc	tcd@cdevnum	equ 1	;position in the CDevItem list@rawcdevnum	equ @cdevnum+2	;position in MemRec (sorted list)@ptr	equ @rawcdevnum+2	jsr LocateCDevNumberA  ;returns path ptr in @ptr	lda <@ptr+2	ldy <@ptr	sta srqPath+2	sty srqPath	lda @rawcdevnum	jsr CalcZoomRect	sta zoomRectPtr+2	sty zoomRectPtr	jsr InvalZoomRect*** If already open, just bring it to the front	lda TheItemPtr+2	ldy TheItemPtr	sta <@ptr+2	sty <@ptr	ldy #oCDevItemWindow+1	lda [<@ptr],y	beq @notAlreadyOpen	iny	lda [<@ptr],y	pha	dey	dey	lda [<@ptr],y	pha	_SelectWindow	brl @exit@notAlreadyOpen;;;	pea cpOpenCDev	pea internalOpenCDev  ;3-Sep-92 DAL	pea $8002	;how = by user ID, stop after acceptance	pea 0	pha	_MMStartUp	;target = my own memory ID	pla	ora #$0100	pha	pushlong #srqParmBlock	pushlong #0	;output buffer	_SendRequest	bcc @1	tax	lda >globalErrorCode	cmp #$ffff	;flag = MachineCDEV returned 0	beq @quietExit	txa	jsr ErrorWindowA@quietExit	brl @exit@1*** Redraw the source icon as Open	jsr InvalZoomAndRedraw*** If Option is down, schedule closing the main window	lda MyTaskMods	and #$0800	;option key	beq @noOption	pha	;space for result	pushlong #CloseMainWindTask	_SchAddTask	pla@noOption@exit	pla	;throw away CDev number	pla	;throw away the raw cdev number	pla	pla	;throw away pointer	pld	rts	entry globalErrorCodeglobalErrorCode	dc.w 0********************************************************************************* CloseMainWindTask -- if the main window is open, close it!********************************************************************************CloseMainWindTask	php	rep #$30	phb	phk	plb	lda MainWindPtr+1	beq @exit	lda MainWindPtr+2	pha	lda MainWindPtr	pha	_CloseNDAByWinPtr@exit	plb	plp	rtl********************************************************************************* ClosingCDevWindow** Inputs:*   LONG  window pointer being closed** Action taken:*   Hide the window and zoom it closed to the right place, if its icon is*     visible.*   Mark the icon closed and invalidate the icon rectangle.*   Zero out the window pointer field of the CDev Item.********************************************************************************	export ClosingCDevWindow	entry FindListIndexClosingCDevWindow	phd	pha	pha	;space for @refcon	pha	pha	;space for @ItemPtr	tsc	tcd@itemPtr	equ 1@refcon	equ @itemPtr+4@oldD	equ @refcon+4@rtl	equ @oldD+2@window	equ @rtl+3	pei <@window+2	pei <@window	_HideWindow	pha	pha	pei <@window+2	pei <@window	_GetWRefCon	pla	sta <@refcon	pla	sta <@refcon+2	ldy #owbCDevItemPtr+1	lda [<@refcon],y	bne @1	brl @noItemStruct@1	ldy #owbCDevItemPtr	lda [<@refcon],y	sta <@itemPtr	iny	iny	lda [<@refcon],y	sta <@itemPtr+2;;;	ldy #owbRawCDevNumber;;;	lda [<@refcon],y*** added 6-Feb-92 DAL -- find the real position of this CDev in the list	lda <@itemPtr+2	ldy <@itemPtr	jsr FindListIndex	ldy #owbRawCDevNumber	sta [<@refcon],y*** end 6-Feb-92	sta TheRawCDevNumber;; zoom closed if possible;; Rect1 = LocalToGlobal on the portrect of @window; Rect2 = the icon's rectangle (calczoomrect);	lda MainWindPtr+1	bne @isOpen	brl @mainWindowClosed@isOpen	pha	pha	_GetPort	pei <@window+2	pei <@window	_SetPort	pushlong #theWindRect	_GetPortRect	pushlong #theWindRect	_LocalToGlobal	pushlong #theWindRect+4	_LocalToGlobal	jsr PushMainWindPtr	_SetPort	pea 0	;flags (zoom closed)	pea 0	;flags (low word)	ldy #owbRawCDevNumber	lda [<@refcon],y	jsr CalcZoomRect	;port must be main window*** added 7-Feb-92 DAL	sta zoomRectPtr+2	sty zoomRectPtr*** end 7-Feb-92	pha	phy	pushlong #theWindRect	_WhooshRect	_SetPort@mainWindowClosed; mark the icon closed@ptr	equ 1	lda ListMemHandle+1	;8-Jul-91 DAL	beq @noListExists	;8-Jul-91 DAL	phd	pushlong ListMemHandle	tsc	tcd	ldy #2	lda [@ptr],y	tax	lda [@ptr]	sta @ptr	stx @ptr+2	pha	pha	;space for _Multiply	lda TheRawCDevNumber	pha	pea LISTMEMSIZE	_Multiply	clc	pla	adc <@ptr	sta <@ptr	pla	adc <@ptr+2	sta <@ptr+2	ldy #oMemState	lda [<@ptr],y	and #$ffff-$0002	;draw the icon as Closed	sta [<@ptr],y	pla	pla	pld@noListExists; invalidate the icon	lda MainWindPtr+1	beq @cantInval	jsr InvalZoomAndRedraw@cantInval	lda #0	ldy #oCDevItemWindow	sta [<@itemPtr],y	iny	iny	sta [<@itemPtr],y@noItemStruct	pla	pla	pla	pla	pld	lda 1,s	sta 1+4,s	lda 2,s	sta 2+4,s	pla	pla	rtltheWindRect	dc.w 0,0,0,0InvalZoomAndRedraw	pha	pha	_GetPort	jsr PushMainWindPtr	_SetPort	jsr InvalZoomRect	jsr ForceMainUpdate	;4-Dec-91 DAL	_SetPort	rts** FindListIndex** Input: AY = CDev item pointer to find*        ListMemHandle*        CDevListCount** Output: A = position of this CDev in the sorted MemRec list (zero based)*FindListIndex	sta @targetItem+2	sty @targetItem	lda #0@loop	pha	jsr @FetchItemPtr	;into AY	cmp @targetItem+2	bne @next	cpy @targetItem	beq @found@next	pla	inc a	cmp CDevListCount	bcc @loop	lda #0	;should never get here!!	rts@found	pla	rts@targetItem	dc.l 0** FetchItemPtr** In: A = index into ListMemHandle** Out: AY = oMemItemPtr for this item*@FetchItemPtr	phd	pha	;index into list	pushlong ListMemHandle	tsc	tcd@list	equ 1@index	equ @list+4	ldy #2	lda [<@list],y	tax	lda [<@list]	sta <@list	stx <@list+2	pha	pha	pea LISTMEMSIZE	pei <@index	_Multiply	clc	pla	adc <@list	sta <@list	pla	adc <@list+2	sta <@list+2	ldy #oMemItemPtr	lda [<@list],y	tax	iny	iny	lda [<@list],y	txy	plx	plx	;pulled list pointer	plx	;pulled index	pld	rts********************************************************************************* InvalZoomRect********************************************************************************InvalZoomRect	lda zoomRectPtr+1	beq @noInval	pushlong zoomRectPtr	pushlong #localZoomRect	pushlong #8	_BlockMove	stz zeropoint	stz zeropoint+2	pushlong #zeropoint	_GlobalToLocal	;convert (0,0) to local coordinates	pushlong #localZoomRect	lda zeropoint+2	pha	lda zeropoint	pha	_OffsetRect	;offset entire rect by same amount	pushlong #localZoomRect	_InvalRect	;invalidate the local rectangle@noInval	rtszeropoint	dc.w 0,0localZoomRect	dc.w 0,0,0,0********************************************************************************* ForceMainUpdate** Update the main window right now, before the user has a chance to scroll* one of their icons out from underneath the invalidated area!********************************************************************************ForceMainUpdate	jsr PushMainWindPtr	_BeginUpdate	jsl MainContentDraw	jsr PushMainWindPtr	_EndUpdate	rts********************************************************************************* LocateCDevNumberA** Inputs: A = CDev number (1=first)** Output: @ptr points to CDev's pathname*         AY points to the CDev's item record** WARNING: Stack frame shared between OpenCDevNumberA, LocateCDevNumberA,*          DerefAYToPtr, and AboutCDevNumberA********************************************************************************LocateCDevNumberA@cdevnum	equ 1	;position in the CDevItem list@rawcdevnum	equ @cdevnum+2	;position in MemRec (sorted list)@ptr	equ @rawcdevnum+2*** get the real CDev number (the one we have now is based on the SORTED list)	lda ListMemHandle+2	ldy ListMemHandle	jsr DerefAYtoPtr	pha	pha	;space for _Multiply	pei @rawcdevnum	;0-based	pea LISTMEMSIZE	_Multiply	clc	pla	adc <@ptr	sta <@ptr	pla	adc <@ptr+2	sta <@ptr+2	ldy #oMemCDevNumber	lda [<@ptr],y	;zero-based	sta <@cdevnum	lda CDevItemsHandle+2	ldy CDevItemsHandle	jsr DerefAYtoPtr	pha	pha	;space for _Multiply result	pei @cdevnum	;CDev number (0-based)	pea CDEVITEMSIZE	_Multiply	clc	pla	adc <@ptr	sta <@ptr	sta TheItemPtr	pla	adc <@ptr+2	sta <@ptr+2	sta TheItemPtr+2	ldy #oCDevItemPathOffset+2	lda [<@ptr],y	pha	dey	dey	lda [<@ptr],y	pha	lda CDevPathsHandle+2	ldy CDevPathsHandle	jsr DerefAYtoPtr	clc	pla	adc <@ptr	sta <@ptr	pla	adc <@ptr+2	sta <@ptr+2	lda TheItemPtr+2	ldy TheItemPtr	rts	export TheItemPtrTheItemPtr	dc.l 0	export TheRawCDevNumberTheRawCDevNumber	dc.w 0********************************************************************************* DerefAYtoPtr -- private to OpenCDevNumberA** @ptr must be 5!** WARNING: Stack frame shared between OpenCDevNumberA, LocateCDevNumberA,*          DerefAYToPtr, and AboutCDevNumberA********************************************************************************DerefAYtoPtr@ptr	equ 5	sta <@ptr+2	sty <@ptr	ldy #2	lda [<@ptr],y	tay	lda [<@ptr]	sta <@ptr	sty <@ptr+2	rts********************************************************************************* Parameter block for the cpOpenCDev request********************************************************************************srqParmBlock	dc.w 4	;parameter countsrqPath	dc.l 0	;pointer to pathnamezoomRectPtr	dc.l 0	;rectangle to zoom from	dc.w CDevFileType	;filetype	dc.l 0	;auxiliary typesmallZoomRect	ds.b 8********************************************************************************* CalcZoomRect** Input:*   CDev number in A (zero based)** Output:*   AY = NIL or pointer to icon rectangle********************************************************************************CalcZoomRect	inc a	sta @num	;1-based number	pha	jsr PushListControl	_GetCtlValue	pla	eor #$ffff	sec	adc @num	bmi @nil	cmp #3	;listView--3 items visible at once	bcs @nil	pha	lda #3	;top	sta smallZoomRect	lda #33+3	;bottom	sta smallZoomRect+4	lda #12	;left	sta smallZoomRect+2	lda #104	;right	sta smallZoomRect+6	pushlong #smallZoomRect	;offset the top left	_LocalToGlobal	pushlong #smallZoomRect+4	;offset the bottom right	_LocalToGlobal	pla	pha	pha	;space for Multiply result	pha	;number of positions down we are	pea 33	;height of CDev item	_Multiply	ply	;amount to offset	plx	pushlong #smallZoomRect	pea 0	;horizontal offset	phy	;vertical offset	_OffsetRect	lda #^smallZoomRect	ldy #smallZoomRect	rts@nil	lda #0	tay	rts@num	dc.w 0********************************************************************************* ErrorWindowA********************************************************************************ErrorWindowA	pha	;space for button	pea 0	;sub type	pea 0	pea 0	;substitution array	pha	;error number	jsr @saveCursor	_ErrorWindow	jsr @restoreCursor	pla	rts@saveCursor	pha	pha	_GetCursorAdr	pla	sta @localCursor	pla	sta @localCursor+2	_InitCursor	rts@restoreCursor	pushlong @localCursor	_SetCursor	rts@localCursor	dc.l 0********************************************************************************* hitHelp -- they want the Help for the selected CDevs********************************************************************************hitHelp	lda #0@loop	pha	;space for NextMember2 result	pha	;item num input	jsr PushListControl	_NextMember2	pla	beq @done	pha	jsr AboutCDevNumberA	pla	bra @loop@done	rts********************************************************************************* AboutCDevNumberA** The CDev they want help with may or may not already be open.** WARNING: Stack frame shared between OpenCDevNumberA, LocateCDevNumberA,*          DerefAYToPtr, and AboutCDevNumberA********************************************************************************AboutCDevNumberA	phd	pha	pha	;space for pointer	dec a	;make cdev number 0-based	pha	;raw cdev number	pha	;translated cdev number	tsc	tcd@cdevnum	equ 1	;position in the CDevItem list@rawcdevnum	equ @cdevnum+2	;position in MemRec (sorted list)@ptr	equ @rawcdevnum+2	lda <@rawcdevnum	jsr LocateCDevNumberA  ;returns path ptr in @ptr, item rec in AY	pei @ptr+2	pei @ptr	;keep path in case we need it	sta @ptr+2	sty @ptr	ldy #oCDevItemWindow+1	lda [@ptr],y	beq @notOpen* it's already open--get reference number from window block	plx	plx	;threw out the pathname pointer	pha	pha	;space for GetWRefCon result	ldy #oCdevItemWindow+2	lda [@ptr],y	pha	dey	dey	lda [@ptr],y	pha	_GetWRefCon	phd	tsc	tcd	ldy #owbResfileNum	lda [3],y	tax	pld	pla	pla	lda #0	;flag = CDev's about box, not ours	jsr DoAboutBox@exit	pla	;throw away CDev number	pla	;throw away the raw cdev number	pla	pla	;throw away pointer	pld	rts** notopen -- pathname pointer already on the stack*@notopen	plx	ply	pha	;space for OpenResourceFile result	pea 1	;read-only access	pushlong #0	;map address	phy	phx	;pathname pointer	jsr GetAndFixPrefs	;3-Dec-91 DAL	_OpenResourceFile	jsr RestorePrefs	;3-Dec-91 DAL	plx	bcs @err	phx	;copy of refnum for CloseResourceFile later	lda #0	;flag = a CDev's about box, not ours	jsr DoAboutBox	;X reg = resource file number	_CloseResourceFile	bra @exit@err	jsr ErrorWindowA	bra @exit********************************************************************************* hitVersion  -- fall into hitAbout********************************************************************************hitVersion********************************************************************************* hitAbout -- they need help with the Control Panel itself********************************************************************************hitAbout	lda #1	;flag = our own About window, not a CDev's	jsr DoAboutBox	rts********************************************************************************* DoAboutBox** Inputs: A = 0 if we should do a CDev's about box*             1 for the main Control Panel about box**         X = resource file reference number if we're doing a CDev about*             (undefined for the CP's about box)********************************************************************************	import IgnoreOneDeactivateDoAboutBox	sta ourAboutFlag	stx aboutCDevResNum	tay	bne @noWaitCur	_WaitCursor@noWaitCur	jsl IgnoreOneDeactivate   ;use the cool color table (17-Mar-93 DAL)	jsr GetExtraTools	stz TheAboutIcon+1*** fix up the window rectangle	lda #25	sta aboutRect+0	;y1	lda #190	sta aboutRect+4	;y2	lda #172	sta aboutRect+2	;x1	lda #464	sta aboutRect+6	;x2	pha	_GetMasterSCB	pla	and #$0080	bne @is640	lda #12	sta aboutRect+2	;x1	lda #306	sta aboutRect+6	;x2@is640	pha	pha	_GetPort	;leave port on stack for @exit*** create our about window	pha	pha	;space for NewWindow result	pushlong #aboutRec	_NewWindow	pla	sta aboutWindow	pla	sta aboutWindow+2	bcc @1	brl @exit@1*** create the OK button	pha	pha	;space for NewControl2 result	jsr pushAboutWindow	pea 3	;pointer to template pointers	pushlong #aboutItems	_NewControl2	pla	pla	;(ignore result)	pha	;preserve resource file & use the CDev	_GetCurResourceFile*** Is it the Control Panel help window?	lda ourAboutFlag	beq @notOurs*** create our help text control	pha	pha	;space for NewControl2 result	jsr pushAboutWindow	pea 0	pushlong #myabout	_NewControl2	pla	pla	;(ignore result)	brl @doneAddingCtls*** let the CDev create its controls@notOurs	lda aboutCDevResNum	pha	_SetCurResourceFile	lda #$ffff	;so we don't do a NewControl2 on it!	sta TheAboutFlags	;(anticipate trouble)	pha	pha	pea rCDevFlags	pushlong #1	_LoadResource	pla	ply	bcs @flagsErr	phy	pha	pushlong #TheAboutFlags	pushlong #aboutFlagsEnd-TheAboutFlags	_HandToPtr	pha	pha	;space for LoadResource result	pea rIcon	pushlong #1	_LoadResource	lda 3,s	pha	lda 3,s	pha	_HLock	phd	tsc	tcd	ldy #2	lda [3],y	sta TheAboutIcon+2	lda [3]	sta TheAboutIcon	pld	pla	pla@flagsErr	lda TheAboutFlags	and #wantAbout	beq @noWantAbout	lda #0	pha	pha	pea AboutCDev	jsr pushAboutWindow	pha	pha	jsl CallTheTopCDev	pla	ply	bra @doneAddingCtls*** the CDev doesn't want to, so we'll use the CDev's rControlList ID=2 resource@noWantAbout	pha	pha	;space for NewControl2 result	jsr pushAboutWindow	pea 9	;resourceToResource	pushlong #2	;rControlList ID=2	_NewControl2	pla	pla	;(ignore result)@doneAddingCtls	pha	pea 1	_WindowGlobal	;make the main window not unhilite when we open the new one	pla	jsr pushAboutWindow	_ShowWindow	_InitCursor	pha	pea $fffe	;re-enable normal window hiliting	_WindowGlobal	pla@modal	pha	pha	;space for DoModalWindow result	pushlong #myTaskRec	pushlong #DrawAbout	;update	pushlong #0	;event hook	pushlong #0	;beep proc	pea 0	;flags	_DoModalWindow	pla	plx	cmp #1000	;OK button hit?	bne @modal	jsr pushAboutWindow	_CloseWindow	_SetCurResourceFile@exit	_SetPort*** added 7-Feb-92 DAL	jsr ReleaseExtraTools*** end 7-Feb-92	_InitCursor	rtspushAboutWindow	plx	pushlong aboutWindow	phx	rtsaboutWindow	dc.l 0ourAboutFlag	dc.w 0aboutCDevResNum	dc.w 0********************************************************************************* GetExtraTools** If Text Edit and Font Manager aren't started, let's start them up so* CDev Help windows can use them cleanly.********************************************************************************GetExtraTools	stz WeLoadedFM	stz WeStartedFM	pea 0	_FMStatus	pla	bcc @present	pea $001b	;Font Mgr	pea $0303	;3.3	_LoadOneTool	bcs @fmDone	inc WeLoadedFM	pea 0	_FMStatus	pla@present	bne @fmDone	pha	_MMStartUp	;id for FMStartUp	jsr GetDirPage	pha	;dp for FMStartUp	stx fmHandle+2	sty fmHandle	_FMStartUp	inc WeStartedFM@fmDone*** Now do the same for Text Edit	stz WeLoadedTE	stz WeStartedTE	pea 0	_TEStatus	pla	bcc @tePresent	pea $0022	;Text Edit	pea $0103	;1.3	_LoadOneTool	bcs @teDone	inc WeLoadedTE	pea 0	_TEStatus	pla@tePresent	bne @teDone	pha	_MMStartUp	;id for TEStartUp	jsr GetDirPage	pha	;dp for TEStartUp	stx teHandle+2	sty teHandle	_TEStartUp	inc WeStartedTE@teDone	rts** GetDirPage -- return handle in XY, pointer in A*GetDirPage	pha	pha	pea 0	pea $0100	;one page	pha	_MMStartUp	;mem id	pea $c015	;attr	pea 0	pea 0	;bank zero	_NewHandle	phd	tsc	tcd	lda [3]	;deref	pld	ply	plx	rts********************************************************************************* ReleaseExtraTools** If we started up Text Edit or Font Manager in GetExtraTools, free them.********************************************************************************ReleaseExtraTools	lda WeStartedTE	beq @noStopTE	_TEShutDown	pushlong teHandle	_DisposeHandle	stz teHandle+1@noStopTE	lda WeLoadedTE	beq @noUnloadTE	pea $0022	;text edit	_UnloadOneTool@noUnloadTE	lda WeStartedFM	beq @noStopFM	_FMShutDown	pushlong fmHandle	_DisposeHandle	stz fmHandle+1@noStopFM	lda WeLoadedFM	beq @noUnloadFM	pea $001b	;font manager	_UnloadOneTool@noUnloadFM	rtsWeLoadedFM	dc.w 0WeStartedFM	dc.w 0WeLoadedTE	dc.w 0WeStartedTE	dc.w 0fmHandle	dc.l 0teHandle	dc.l 0********************************************************************************* CallTheTopCDev -- transfer control to the CDev whose code is in the*                   current resource file** If there's a problem, then strip the 10 bytes of inputs to the CDev* routine and just return.********************************************************************************CallTheTopCDev	pha	pha	pea rCDevCode	pushlong #1	_LoadResource	bcs @strip	phd	tsc	tcd	lda [3]	sta @toTheCDev+1	ldy #1	lda [3],y	sta @toTheCDev+2	pld	pla	pla@toTheCDev	jml >$777777@strip	pla	pla	;pulled LoadResource result	lda 2,s	sta 2+10,s	lda 1,s	sta 1+10,s	pla	pla	pla	pla	pla	rtl*******************************************************************************aboutRec	dc.w aboutEnd-aboutRec  ; param length	dc.w $2000	; wFrame	dc.l 0	; wTitle	dc.l 0	; wRefCon	dc.w 0,0,0,0	; wZoom top,left,bottom,right	dc.l 0	; wColor	dc.w 0	; wYOrigin	dc.w 0	; wXOrigin	dc.w 0	; wDataH	dc.w 0	; wDataW	dc.w 0	; wMaxH	dc.w 0	; wMaxW	dc.w 0	; wScrollVer	dc.w 0	; wScrollHor	dc.w 0	; wPageVer	dc.w 0	; wPageHor	dc.l 0	; wInfoRefCon	dc.w 0	; wInfoHeight	dc.l 0	; wFrameDefProc	dc.l 0	; wInfoDefProc	dc.l 0	; wContDefProc (DrawAbout will be used)aboutRect	dc.w 25,0,190,320	; wPosition top,left,right,bottom	dc.l -1	; wPlane	dc.l 0	; wStorageaboutEnd** Control list for the About window*aboutItems	dc.l Okay	dc.l 0** Simple button: OK*Okay	dc.w 9	dc.L 1000	dc.w 146,20+84,160,100+84	dc.L $80000000	dc.w 1	dc.w $3000	dc.L 0	dc.L TheTitle	dc.L 0	dc.b 13,13	;key equivalents	dc.w 0	dc.w 0TheTitle	dc.b 2,'OK'** stat text control for the main CP about text*myabout	dc.w 9	;pcount	dc.l 5		dc.w 10,0,135,290	dc.l $81000000	;stat text	dc.w 0	dc.w $1000	dc.l 0 	dc.l abt	dc.w abtL	dc.w 1abt	dc.b 1,'S',16,0	dc.b 'Control Panel 2.1',13	dc.b 1,'S',0,0	dc.b 'by',13	dc.b 'Dave “Mr Tangent” Lyons',13	dc.b 13	dc.b 'Some portions by',13	dc.b 'Michael Stein',13	dc.b 'and',13	dc.b 'Darryl Lovato',13	dc.b 13	dc.b 'Copyright (C) 1990-1993',13	dc.b 'Apple Computer, Inc.',13	dc.b 'All Rights Reserved',13abtL	equ *-abt********************************************************************************* DrawAbout********************************************************************************DrawAbout	phb	phk	plb	lda #2	pha	pha	_SetPenSize	pea 0	pea 139	_MoveTo	pea 500	pea 139	_LineTo	lda #1	pha	pha	_SetPenSize	lda TheAboutIcon+1	beq @noIcon	pushlong TheAboutIcon	pea 0	;mode	pea 6	;X position (was 4 in CP 1.x)	pea 3	;Y position	_DrawIcon@noIcon	lda aboutRect+6	;right edge	sec	sbc aboutRect+2	;left edge	lsr a	sta aboutCenter	lda ourAboutFlag	beq @1	brl @skipStrings@1	pha	pushlong #aflagName	_StringWidth	pla	jsr Center	pha	pea 11	_MoveTo	pushlong #aflagName	_DrawString	pha	pushlong #byStr	_StringWidth	pla	jsr Center	pha	pea 21	_MoveTo	pushlong #byStr	_DrawString	pha	pushlong #aflagAuthor	_StringWidth	pla	jsr Center	pha	pea 31	_MoveTo	pushlong #aflagAuthor	_DrawString	pha	pushlong #aflagVersionStr	_StringWidth	pla	eor #$ffff	sec	adc aboutRect+6	sec	sbc aboutRect+2	sec	sbc #5	pha	pea 10	_MoveTo	pushlong #aflagVersionStr	_DrawString@skipStrings	pha	pha	_GetPort	_DrawControls	plb	rtlCenter	lsr a	eor #$ffff	sec	adc aboutCenter	rtsaboutCenter	dc.w 0TheAboutIcon	dc.l 0TheAboutFlagsaTheFlags	dc.w 0aflagEnabled	dc.b 0aflagVersion	dc.b 0aflagMachine	dc.b 0aflagReserved	dc.b 0aflagDataRect	dc.w 0,0,0,0aflagName	ds.b 16aflagAuthor	ds.b 33aflagVersionStr	ds.b 9AboutFlagsEndbyStr	dc.b 2,'by'********************************************************************************* hitList********************************************************************************hitList	jsr SetButtonStates	lda myTaskWhat	cmp #1	;mouse down?	bne @ignoreHit	lda myClickCount	cmp #2	bcc @ignoreHit	lda theOpenButtonState	cmp #$00ff	beq @ignoreHit	lda #2	jsr HiliteOpen	;blink Open button on	lda #0	jsr HiliteOpen	;blink Open button off	jsr hitOpen@ignoreHit	rts********************************************************************************* SetButtonStates** See if there are any CDevs selected in the list.  If so, enable the Open* and CDev-help buttons.  If not, disable them.********************************************************************************SetButtonStates	lda #0	pha	;space for NextMember2 result	pha	;item num input	jsr PushListControl	_NextMember2	pla	beq @disable*** Enable Help only if exactly 1 icon selected	pha	pha	;item num input	jsr PushListControl	_NextMember2	pla	beq @enable	;enable them both (no more selected icons)	pea $00ff	;hilite state for Help button	pea $0000	;hilite state for Open button	bra @EnableJustOne@disable	lda #$00ff	bra @enableOrDisable@enable	lda #0@enableOrDisable	pha	;0 to enable, $FF to disable	pha@EnableJustOne	lda 1,s	sta theOpenButtonState	lda #OpenControlID	jsr PushCtlHandle	_HiliteControl	lda #CDevHelpControlID	jsr PushCtlHandle	_HiliteControl	rts********************************************************************************* PushCtlHandle** Input: control ID in A (for some control in the main window)********************************************************************************PushCtlHandle	pha	pha	;space for result (and temporary storage!)	jsr PushMainWindPtr	lda 5,s	pea 0	pha	_GetCtlHandleFromID	pla	;move result under return address	ply	plx	phy	pha	phx	rts********************************************************************************* HiliteOpen** Input:  part code in A (2 to hilite the Open button, 0 to unhilite it)********************************************************************************HiliteOpen	pha	;hilite value	sta theOpenButtonState	lda #OpenControlID	jsr PushCtlHandle	_HiliteControl	rtstheOpenButtonState	dc.w 0********************************************************************************* Task record********************************************************************************myTaskRecmyTaskWhat	dc.w 0myTaskMsg	dc.l 0	dc.l 0	;whenmyTaskWhere	dc.w 0,0myTaskMods	dc.w 0myTaskData	dc.l 0myTaskMask	dc.l $001fffff	;everything (5.0.3)	dc.l 0	;lastClickTickmyClickCount	dc.w 0	;click countmyTaskData2	dc.l 0	;task data 2myTaskData3	dc.l 0	;task data 3myTaskData4	dc.l 0	;task data 4	dc.w 0,0	;last click point********************************************************************************* SpecialEventHandling** Input:  event record pointer at <1** If this is a Command-Control-Esc event, handle it and make the event* into a null event.********************************************************************************	export SpecialEventHandlingSpecialEventHandling@event	equ 1	lda [<@event]	cmp #3	;is it a keyDown?	bne @failed	ldy #2	;offset to event Message	lda [<@event],y	and #$00ff	cmp #$001b	;Escape?	bne @failed*** Require the Shift key & not the Control or Option keys	ldy #14	;offset to event modifiers	lda [<@event],y	and #$1300	;ctrl+option+shift+apple	cmp #$0300	;apple+shift	bne @failed	jsr OpenMyself	lda #0	sta [<@event]@failed	rtl**************************************************************************************************************************************************************** InstallRequestProc********************************************************************************InstallRequestProc** First, let's stuff our memory ID into our AcceptRequests string to* make it unique (in case there is more than one copy of the Control* panel in the machine).*	pha	pha	pha	;space for MMStartUp result	_MMStartUp	_HexIt	pla	sta ReqProcHexID	pla	sta ReqProcHexID+2	ldx #^CtlPanelRequestProc	ldy #CtlPanelRequestProc	bra instOrRemoveRQ********************************************************************************* RemoveRequestProc********************************************************************************RemoveRequestProc	ldx #0	txyinstOrRemoveRQ	pushlong #ReqProcName	lda MyMemID	pha	phx	phy	;nil or ReqProc ptr	_AcceptRequests	rtsReqProcName	dc.b 25,'Apple~Control Panel~'ReqProcHexID	dc.b 'xxxx~'********************************************************************************* CtlPanelRequestProc** This is called by the Tool Locator SendRequest call.* For example, the Finder calls SendRequest when the user* tries to open documents and the Finder doesn't know how.********************************************************************************CtlPanelRequestProc	name@oldDPage	equ 1@RTL1	equ 3@DataOut	equ 6@DataIn	equ 10@Request	equ 14@Result	equ 16@InputSize	equ 10	;request procs must clean 10 bytes from the stack	phd	tsc	tcd	phb	phk	plb	lda <@Request	sta @requestTable	ldx #@requestTableEnd-@requestTable@loop	dex	dex	dex	dex	cmp @requestTable,x	bne @loop		jsr (@requestTable+2,x)	ror <@Result	;rotate accept flag into bit 15	plb	pld	lda 2,s	;clean InputSize bytes off the stack	sta 2+@InputSize,s	lda 1,s	sta 1+@InputSize,s	ply	ply	ply	ply	ply	rtl********************************************************************************* Request Table has one entry per request code that we handle.* The first entry catches anything we don't match, so it has* the "null" handler that never claims the request.** Each request handler returns CLC if it didn't handle the* request, SEC if it did.********************************************************************************@requestTable	dc.w $7777	dc.w    @handleOther	dc.w finderSaysBeforeOpen	dc.w    @handleBeforeOpen*** added 3-Sep-92 DAL to fix bug introduced in 6.0.1d9	dc.w internalOpenCDev	dc.w    @handleOpenCDev*** end 3-Sep-92	dc.w cpOpenCDev	dc.w    @handleBeforeOpen	;29-Jul-92 DAL (was @handleOpenCDev in 6.0)	dc.w systemSaysMenuKey	dc.w    @handleMenuKey	dc.w cpOpenControlPanels	dc.w    @handleOpenControlPanels@requestTableEnd@handleOther	clc	rts********************************************************************************* handleBeforeOpen** The Finder wants us to open some documents.** If these are CDev documents, let's try to open them.** DataIn points to the following structure:*   +000 WORD  parameter count (in 6.0, 6 means 7)*   +002 LONG  pointer to class-one pathname*   +006 LONG  pointer to rectangle to zoom from (NIL if none appropriate) *   +010 WORD  filetype*   +012 LONG  auxtype*   +016 WORD  modifiers*   +018 LONG  Finder icon handle*   +022 WORD  printFlag (0=open)********************************************************************************@handleBeforeOpen	ldy #oFiletype	lda [<@dataIn],y	;check filetype = CDEV	cmp #CDevFileType	bne @notCDev*** 29-Jul-92 DAL -- see if there's a printFlag to check	lda [<@dataIn]	cmp #7	bcc @noPrintFlag*** end 29-Jul-92*** make sure this is an Open, not a Print	ldy #oPrintFlag	lda [<@dataIn],y	bne @notCDev@noPrintFlag	lda #0	sta >TheItemPtr	sta >TheItemPtr+2	sta >TheRawCDevNumber  ;6-Feb-92 DAL	jsr @handleOpenCDev	bcs @success	lda >globalErrorCode	cmp #$ffff	;sets carry if MachineCDev failed@success*** invalidate the list in the main window if we opened anything	php	pha	lda MainWindPtr+1	beq @noMainWindow*** 15-Jul-92 DAL -- use new InvalOneCtlByID call	jsr PushMainWindPtr	pushlong #ListControlID	ldx #$3E10	jsl $e10000;	_InvalOneCtlByID*** end 15-Jul-92@noMainWindow	pla	plp	rts@notCDev	clc	rts********************************************************************************* handleOpenCDev** DataIn points to the following structure:*   +000 WORD  parameter count (at least 4)*   +002 LONG  pointer to class-one pathname*   +006 LONG  pointer to rectangle to zoom from (NIL if none appropriate) *   +010 WORD  filetype*   +012 LONG  auxtype** >TheItemPtr points to the CDevItem structure for this CDev, if any.********************************************************************************	import OpenNewCDevAY@handleOpenCDev	lda #0	sta >globalErrorCode	pha	pha	_GetCursorAdr	pla	sta @openOldCursor	pla	sta @openOldCursor+2	ldy #oSmallRect+2	lda [<@dataIn],y	pha	dey	dey	lda [<@dataIn],y	pha	ldy #oPathname+2	lda [<@dataIn],y	pha	dey	dey	lda [<@dataIn],y	tay	pla	jsl OpenNewCDevAY	;takes rectangle pointer on stack, returns TheCDevWindow in AY	pha	phy	pushlong @openOldCursor	_SetCursor	pla	;see if result (LONG on stack) is NIL	ora 1,s	plx	tax	beq @failed	sec	rts@failed	clc	rts@openOldCursor	dc.l 0********************************************************************************* handleMenuKey** DataIn points to the Task Record for the keyDown event********************************************************************************@handleMenuKey	ldy #2	;offset to event Message	lda [<@dataIn],y	and #$00ff	cmp #$001b	;Escape?	bne @failed*** Require the Shift key & not the Control or Option keys	ldy #14	;offset to event modifiers	lda [<@dataIn],y	and #$1300	;ctrl+option+shift+apple	cmp #$0300	;apple+shift	bne @failed	jsr OpenMyself	sec	;claim the request	rts********************************************************************************* handleOpenControlPanels** Open the main Control Panels window********************************************************************************@handleOpenControlPanels	jsr OpenMyself	sec	;claim the request	rts********************************************************************************* OpenMyself -- call OpenNDA on myself, hiliting the first menu in*               the current menu bar (I hope that's the Apple menu!)********************************************************************************OpenMyself	pea $8000	;for HiliteMenu($8000,x) later (23-Nov-92 DAL)	jsr GetFirstMenuID	pha	;menu id for HiliteMenu(0,x) later	pea $8001	;for HiliteMenu($8001,x) (23-Nov-92 DAL)	pha	;menu ID	_HiliteMenu	pha	;space for OpenNDA result	jsl GetMyMainMenuID	pha	_OpenNDA	pla	_HiliteMenu	;HiliteMenu($8000,x)	rts** GetFirstMenuID--return ID of first menu in A*GetFirstMenuID	pha	pha	;space for GetMHandle result	pea 0	;get first menu handle	_GetMHandle	phd	tsc	tcd	ldy #2	lda [3],y	tax	lda [3]	sta 3	stx 5	lda [3]	pld	plx	plx	rts**************************************************************************************************************************************************************** Miscellaneous subroutines********************************************************************************GetAndFixPrefs	_GetSysPrefsGS oldPrefs	lda oldPrefs+2	and #$1fff	;keep the reserved bits	ora #$C000	;turn on Use Volume Mount Dialog		;no Cancel button! 3-Dec-91 DAL	sta myPrefs+2	_SetSysPrefsGS myPrefs	rtsRestorePrefs	php	pha	_SetSysPrefsGS oldPrefs	pla	plp	rtsoldPrefs	dc.w 1	;1 parameter	dc.w 0	;the old SysPrefsmyPrefs	dc.w 1	dc.w 0	;my modified preferences**************************************************************************************************************************************************************** GetCDevList** Inputs:*   none** Outputs:*   Sets up CDevItemsHandle, CDevPathsHandle, CDevIconsHandle if they*   are not already set up.********************************************************************************	export GetCDevListGetCDevList*** added 6-Feb-92 DAL	lda CDevItemsHandle+1	bne @gotIt*** end 6-Feb-92	jsr ReadExistingDataFile	bcs @rebuildList* validate the list against the actual CDevs directory	jsl DoValidationScan	bcc @gotIt@rebuildList	jsl ScanForCDevs	jsr WriteDataFile@gotIt	rtl********************************************************************************* ReadExistingDatafile** Returns CLC if we read a valid (up-to-date) file into the handles********************************************************************************ReadExistingDataFile	stz dataFileRef3	lda #1	;read only	sta dataFileReqAcc	_OpenGS dataFileOpen	bcs @nope	lda dataFileRef	sta dataFileRef2	sta dataFileRef3	lda #^CDevListSigBuffer	ldy #CDevListSigBuffer	sta dataReadWhere+2	sty dataReadWhere	lda #0	ldy #6	sta dataReadAmount+2	sty dataReadAmount	_ReadGS dataFileRead	bcs @nope* need to validate the signature stuff!	lda CDevListSigBuffer	cmp #$5644	;'DV'	bne @nope	lda CDevListSigBuffer+2	cmp #1	bne @nope	jsr ReadNewHandle	sta CDevItemsHandle+2	sty CDevItemsHandle	bcs @nope	jsr ReadNewHandle	sta CDevPathsHandle+2	sty CDevPathsHandle	bcs @nope	jsr ReadNewHandle	sta CDevIconsHandle+2	sty CDevIconsHandle	bcc @otay@nope	sec@otay	php	pha*** Don't Close(0) if we failed to open	lda dataFileRef3	beq @noClose	_CloseGS dataFileClose@noClose	pla	plp	bcc @keepIt	pha	jsl DisposeCDevList	;dispose of any handles we allocated	pla	sec	rts@keepIt	lda CDevListSigBuffer	sta CDevListSignature	lda CDevListSigBuffer+2	sta CDevListSignature+2	lda CDevListSigBuffer+4	sta CDevListSignature+4	clc	rtsCDevListSigBuffer	ds.b CDEVLISTHEADERSIZEReadNewHandle	lda #^howMuch	ldy #howMuch	sta dataReadWhere+2	sty dataReadWhere	lda #0	ldy #4	sta dataReadAmount+2	sty dataReadAmount	_ReadGS dataFileRead	lda howMuch+2	ldy howMuch	sta dataReadAmount+2	sty dataReadAmount	;leave size needed in AY	pha	pha	;space for NewHandle result	pha	phy	;size needed	jsr PushDataID	pea $C000	;locked and fixed		pha	pha	;location (ignored)	_NewHandle	bcs @error	phd	tsc	tcd	ldy #2	;dereference into Read parmblock	lda [3],y	sta dataReadWhere+2	lda [3]	sta dataReadWhere	pld	_ReadGS dataFileRead@error	ply	pla	;return handle in AY	rtshowMuch	dc.l 0********************************************************************************* WriteDataFile** Try to Create, Open, and Write the data file********************************************************************************WriteDataFile	_CreateGS dataFileCreate	bcc @okay	cmp #$47	;duplicate filename	beq @exists	sec	rts*** 16-Mar-92 DAL -- the old file may be locked--must unlock it@exists	_SetFileInfoGS dataFileCreate*** end 16-Mar-92@okay	stz dataFileRef3	;anticipate failure to open (16-Mar-92 DAL)	lda #3	;read/write	sta dataFileReqAcc	_OpenGS dataFileOpen	bcs @nope	lda dataFileRef	sta dataFileRef2	sta dataFileRef3	lda #^CDevListSignature	ldy #CDevListSignature	sta dataReadWhere+2	sty dataReadWhere	lda #0	ldy #6	sta dataReadAmount+2	sty dataReadAmount	_WriteGS dataFileRead	lda CDevItemsHandle+2	ldy CDevItemsHandle	jsr WriteAHandle	bcs @closeAndKill	lda CDevPathsHandle+2	ldy CDevPathsHandle	jsr WriteAHandle	bcs @closeAndKill	lda CDevIconsHandle+2	ldy CDevIconsHandle	jsr WriteAHandle	bcs @closeAndKill@nope	php	lda dataFileRef3	beq @noClose	_CloseGS dataFileClose@noClose	plp	rts@closeAndKill	pha	_CloseGS dataFileClose	_DestroyGS dataFileDestroy	pla	sec	rtsWriteAHandle	pha	phy	;push copy of handle	pha	pha	;space for GetHandleSize	pha	phy	;handle	_GetHandleSize	pla	sta howMuch	pla	sta HowMuch+2	lda #^howMuch	ldy #howMuch	sta dataReadWhere+2	sty dataReadWhere	lda #0	ldy #4	sta dataReadAmount+2	sty dataReadAmount	_WriteGS dataFileRead	bcs @fail	lda howMuch+2	ldy howMuch	sta dataReadAmount+2	sty dataReadAmount	;leave size needed in AY	phd	tsc	tcd	ldy #2	;dereference into Read parmblock	lda [3],y	sta dataReadWhere+2	lda [3]	sta dataReadWhere	pld	_WriteGS dataFileRead;;;	bcc @cleanExit@fail@cleanExit	ply	pla	;pull copy of handle	rts*******************************************************************************dataFileOpen	dc.w 3dataFileRef	dc.w 0	dc.l dataFilePathdataFileReqAcc	dc.w $7777	;requested accessdataFilePath	dc.w 24	dc.b '*:System:CDevs:CDev.Data'dataFileRead	dc.w 4	;4 parametersdataFileRef2	dc.w 0dataReadWhere	dc.l 0dataReadAmount	dc.l 0	dc.l 0	;amount actually readdataFileClose	dc.w 1	;1 parameterdatafileRef3	dc.w 0dataFileDestroy	dc.w 1	dc.l dataFilePath*** Note: dataFileCreate is used for CreateGS *and* SetFileInfoGSdataFileCreate	dc.w 3	dc.l dataFilePath	dc.w $00E7	;access (invisible = $0004 bit)	dc.w CDevDataFileType**************************************************************************************************************************************************************CDevListSignature	dc.w $5644	;'DV'CDevListVersion	dc.w $0001	export CDevListCountCDevListCount	dc.w 0	;number of CDevs in list	export CDevItemsHandleCDevItemsHandle	dc.l 0	export CDevPathsHandleCDevPathsHandle	dc.l 0	export CDevIconsHandleCDevIconsHandle	dc.l 0	export ListMemHandleListMemHandle	dc.l 0**************************************************************************************************************************************************************** DisposeListMemHndl********************************************************************************DisposeListMemHndl	lda ListMemHandle+1	beq @4	pushlong ListMemHandle	_DisposeHandle	stz ListMemHandle+1@4	rtl********************************************************************************* DisposeCDevList*********************************************************************************** added 6-Feb-92 DAL -- Don't get rid of stuff we still need!	export CondDisposeCDevListCondDisposeCDevList	lda NumCDevsOpen	bne dontKill	lda MainWindPtr+1	bne dontKill*** end 6-Feb-92DisposeCDevList	stz CDevListCount	lda CDevIconsHandle+1	beq @1	pushlong CDevIconsHandle	_DisposeHandle	stz CDevIconsHandle+1@1	lda CDevPathsHandle+1	beq @2	pushlong CDevPathsHandle	_DisposeHandle	stz CDevPathsHandle+1@2	lda CDevItemsHandle+1	beq @3	pushlong CDevItemsHandle	_DisposeHandle	stz CDevItemsHandle+1@3dontKill	rtl********************************************************************************* DoValidationScan** Return CLC if the data file we already read in matches the current set* of CDevs in the *:System:CDevs folder** Comparision data is in CDevItemsHandle; there should be the same number* as in CDevListSigBuffer+oCDevListCount*********************************************************************************DoValidationScan	lda #8	jsr getPfx	phy	phx	lda #0	jsr getPfx	phy	phx	_SetPrefixGS setZeroNull	_SetPrefixGS setEightCdevDir	stz ValidCount	;how many have we found so far?	stz ItemArrayOffset	;which one are we looking at?	jsr OpenDirectory	php	bcs @fail	;@fail requires carry status on stack	plp@next	jsr GetNextCDev	bcs @done	inc ValidCount	jsr ValidateCDevEntry	bcc @next	sec	bra @closeAndExit** Ran out of CDevs--see if the counts match!*@done	lda validCount	cmp CDevListSigBuffer+oCDevListCount	sec	bne @closeAndExit	clc@closeAndExit	php	jsr CloseDirectory@fail	plp	plx	;restore prefix 0	ply	php	lda #0	jsr setPfx	plp	plx	;restore prefix 8	ply	php	lda #8	jsr setPfx	plp	;clc if successful	rtlvalidCount	dc.w 0ItemArrayOffset	dc.w 0	;offset into CDevItemsHandle** ValidateCDevEntry** Inputs:*   entCreateDate (8 bytes)*   CDev Item record at [CDevItemsHandle],ItemArrayOffset+oCDevItemCreateDate** Returns SEC if the dates do not match.* Otherwise increments ItemArrayOffset and returns CLC.*ValidateCDevEntry	phd	pushlong CDevItemsHandle	tsc	tcd	ldy #2	lda [1],y	tax	lda [1]	clc	adc ItemArrayOffset	bcc @1	inx@1	clc	adc #oCDevItemCreateDate	bcc @2	inx@2	sta 1	stx 3		ldy #8	;compare 8 bytes@compare	dey	dey	bmi @equal	lda entCreateDate,y	cmp [1],y	beq @compare	sec	bra @compared@equal	clc@compared	pla	pla	pld	bcs @fail;	clc	lda ItemArrayOffset	adc #CDEVITEMSIZE	sta ItemArrayOffset	clc@fail	rts********************************************************************************* ScanForCDevs********************************************************************************ScanForCDevs	jsl DisposeCDevList	;added 1-Apr-91 DAL	lda #8	jsr getPfx	phy	phx	lda #0	jsr getPfx	phy	phx	jsr NewEmptyHandle	sta CDevItemsHandle+2	sty CDevItemsHandle	jsr NewEmptyHandle	sta CDevPathsHandle+2	sty CDevPathsHandle	jsr NewEmptyHandle	sta CDevIconsHandle+2	sty CDevIconsHandle	_SetPrefixGS setZeroNull	_SetPrefixGS setEightCdevDir	stz CDevListCount	jsr OpenDirectory	bcs @fail@next	jsr GetNextCDev	bcs @done	jsr AppendCDev	bra @next@done	jsr CloseDirectory@fail*** lock down the handles;	_CompactMem	pushlong CDevIconsHandle	_HLock	pushlong CDevItemsHandle	_HLock	pushlong CDevPathsHandle	_HLock*** restore prefix 0	plx	ply	lda #0	jsr setPfx*** restore prefix 8	plx	ply	lda #8	jsr setPfx	rtl********************************************************************************* NewEmptyHandle: output handle in AY********************************************************************************NewEmptyHandle	pha	pha	;space for NewHandle result	lda #0	pha	pha	jsr PushDataID	pea 0	;attributes	pha	pha	;location (ignored)	_NewHandle	ply	pla	rtsPushDataID	pha	;space for MMStartUp result	_MMStartUp	pla	ora #$0700	plx	pha	phx	rts********************************************************************************* OpenDirectory********************************************************************************OpenDirectory	_OpenGS OpenCDevDir	bcs @done	lda dirRef	sta dirRef2	sta dirRef3@done	rts********************************************************************************* GetNextCDev********************************************************************************GetNextCDev	_GetDirEntryGS GetDirEnt	bcs @err	lda entType	cmp #CDevFileType	bne GetNextCDev	lda entAuxType	bmi GetNextCDev	;CDev is inactive	clc@err	rts********************************************************************************* CloseDirectory********************************************************************************CloseDirectory	_CloseGS CloseCDevDir	rts********************************************************************************* AppendCDev********************************************************************************AppendCDev	pha	;space for OpenResourceFile result	pea 1	;read-only	pushlong #0	;map address = NIL	pushlong #theFileName	jsr GetAndFixPrefs	_OpenResourceFile	jsr RestorePrefs	pla	bcs @exit	pha	pha	pea 1	_SetResourceFileDepth ;leave old depth on stack	jsr AppendGuts	pla	;previous depth	pha	;space for SetResourceFileDepth result	pha	;new depth	_SetResourceFileDepth	pla	;throw away old depth (1)	_CloseResourceFile	;refnum still on stack@exit	rtsAppendGuts	pha	pha	pea rCDevFlags	pushlong #1	_LoadResource	plx	ply	phy	phx	pushlong #itemFlags	pushlong #FLAGSSIZE	_HandToPtr*** Put the CDev's create date in the data file	ldy #6@copyCreateDate	lda entCreateDate,y	sta CDevItemTemplate+oCDevItemCreateDate,y	dey	dey	bpl @copyCreateDate*** If there are blanks on the beginning of the CDev name, kill them@stripBlanks	lda CDevItemTemplate+oCDevItemName	and #$00ff	beq @noBlank	lda CDevItemTemplate+oCDevItemName+1	and #$00ff	cmp #$0020	bne @noBlank	pushlong #CDevItemTemplate+oCDevItemName+2 ;source	pushlong #CDevItemTemplate+oCDevItemName+1 ;dest	pushlong #14	_BlockMove	dec CDevItemTemplate+oCDevItemName	;decrement length	bra @stripBlanks@noBlank	pha	pha	pea rIcon	pushlong #1	_LoadResource	pla	sta @iconHandle	pla	sta @iconHandle+2	pha	pha	pushlong CDevIconsHandle	_GetHandleSize	pla	sta iconOffset	pla	sta iconOffset+2		pha	pha	pushlong CDevPathsHandle	_GetHandleSize	pla	sta pathOffset	pla	sta pathOffset+2	pushlong @iconHandle	pushlong CDevIconsHandle	jsr AppendHandle	clc	lda CDevDirectory	adc theFilename	sta theLengthWord	pea 2	pushlong #theLengthWord	pushlong CDevPathsHandle	jsr AppendSomeData	pushword CDevDirectory	pushlong #CDevDirectory+2	pushlong CDevPathsHandle	jsr AppendSomeData	pushword theFilename	pushlong #theFilename+2	pushlong CDevPathsHandle	jsr AppendSomeData	pushword itemSize	pushlong #CDevItemTemplate	pushlong CDevItemsHandle	jsr AppendSomeData	inc CDevListCount	rts@iconHandle	dc.l 0CDevItemTemplateitemSize	dc.w endOfItem-CDevItemTemplateitemDate	ds.b 8pathOffset	dc.l 0iconOffset	dc.l 0itemState	dc.w 0itemWindow	dc.l 0itemFlags	ds.b FLAGSSIZEendOfItemtheLengthWord	dc.w 0	;total length of CDev pathCDevDirectory	dc.w 15	dc.b '*:System:CDevs:'** AppendHandle** Input:*   HANDLE  data to append*   HANDLE  theHandle*AppendHandle	phd	tsc	tcd@oldD	equ 1@rts	equ @oldD+2@theHandle	equ @rts+2@data	equ @theHandle+4	pha	pha	pei @theHandle+2	pei @theHandle	_GetHandleSize	lda 3,s	pha	lda 3,s	pha	pha	pha	pei @data+2	pei @data	_GetHandleSize	clc	pla	adc 3,s	tax	pla	adc 3,s	ply	ply	pha	phx	pei @theHandle+2	pei @theHandle	_SetHandleSize	ldy #2	clc	pla	adc [@theHandle]	tax	pla	adc [@theHandle],y	pei @data+2	pei @data	;source handle	pha	phx	;dest pointer	pha	pha	pei @data+2	pei @data	_GetHandleSize	;length	_HandToPtr	pld	plx	ply	ply	ply	ply	phx	rts** AppendSomeData** Input:*   WORD     size of data to append*   POINTER  data to append*   HANDLE   theHandle*AppendSomeData	phd	tsc	tcd@oldD	equ 1@rts	equ @oldD+2@theHandle	equ @rts+2@data	equ @theHandle+4@size	equ @data+4	pha	pha	pei @theHandle+2	pei @theHandle	_GetHandleSize	lda 3,s	pha	lda 3,s	pha	clc	lda @size	adc 1,s	sta 1,s	lda 3,s	adc #0	sta 3,s	pei @theHandle+2	pei @theHandle	_SetHandleSize	ldy #2	lda [@theHandle],y	tax	lda [@theHandle]	clc	adc 1,s	tay	txa	adc 3,s	plx	plx	;discard	pei @data+2	pei @data	;source	pha	phy	;destination	pea 0	pei @size	;size	_BlockMove	pld	plx	ply	ply	ply	ply	ply	phx	rts********************************************************************************* muck with prefixes 0 and 8********************************************************************************setZeroNull	dc.w 2	dc.w 0	dc.l nullPathnullPath	dc.w 0setEightCDevDir	dc.w 2	dc.w 8	dc.l CDevDirPathCDevDirPath	dc.w 14	dc.b '*:System:CDevs'OpenCDevDir	dc.w 3dirRef	dc.w 0	dc.l CDevDirPath	dc.w $0001	;read onlyCloseCDevDir	dc.w 1dirRef3	dc.w 0GetDirEnt	dc.w 13dirRef2	dc.w 0	dc.w 0,1,1	;flags, base, displacement	dc.l fileNameBuff	dc.w 0	;entry numentType	dc.w 0	;filetype	dc.l 0	;eof	dc.l 0	;blocksentCreateDate	dc.l 0,0	;create date/timeentModDate	dc.l 0,0	;mod date/time	dc.w 0	;accessentAuxType	dc.l 0	;auxtypefileNameBuff	dc.w 34theFileName	ds.b 32;############################################################;#;# getPfx - retrieves current prefix for the supplied;# prefix number.  The handle to the stored prefix is;# returned to the caller.;#;# on entry:;#     Acc = prefix number;#;# on exit:;#     X, Y = handle of stored prefix (low,high);#;############################################################getPfx@tmpPtr	equ $01@pfxHndl	equ $05 	;handle to stored prefix	sta prefixNum	;put prefix number in parmblock (for later)	pha	;make space for temp pointer	pha	pha	;and prefix handle	pha	tsc	;make stack frame	phd	tcd		pha	;make space for NewHandle call	pha	pea 0	;size of block to create	pea 256	;we'll try 256 bytes at first	pha	_MMStartUp	pea $8010	;attributes	pha	;location pointer	pha	;(not used)	_NewHandle	;go get some memory	pla	;retreive handle	plx	bcc @got_mem@memerr	lda #0	pha	;oops!  put up an ErrorWindow	pha	;subString type (not used)	pha	;subStringPtr (not used)	pha	pea $8D	;"Memory is full"	bra @showErr@got_mem	sta @pfxHndl	;save for return to caller	stx @pfxHndl+2	ldy #2	;dereference handle	lda [@pfxHndl]	sta @tmpPtr	sta bufPtr	lda [@pfxHndl],y	sta @tmpPtr+2	sta bufPtr+2	lda #256	;initialize length of buffer	sta [@tmpPtr];;;	lda #2	;set up parm block;;;	sta pCount	;prefixNum set up above@try_again	_GetPrefixGS parmBlock	;get the current prefix	bcc @got_prefix	;no error, continue	cmp #$4f	;buffer too small?	beq @grow_buf	;yes, grow the buffer and try again	pha	;else just puke!	pea 0	;subString type (not used)	pea 0	;subStringPtr (not used)	pea 0	pha	;put error code on stack@showErr	_ErrorWindow	pla	;;retrieve button number	sec	;we had a problem	bra @exit	;just exit@grow_buf	ldy #2	lda [@tmpPtr],y	;get returned length word	clc	adc #4	;allow for length words	pha	;save new length on stack	pea 0	;high word of new size allocation	pha	;low word of length	pei @pfxHndl+2	;put handle on stack	pei @pfxHndl	ldy #4	;unlock the handle first	lda [@pfxHndl],y	asl a	lsr a	;cleared bit 15	sta [@pfxHndl],y	_SetHandleSize	;make the block bigger	bcs @memerr	;abort on error	ldy #4	;lock it down again	lda [@pfxHndl],y	ora #$8000	sta [@pfxHndl],y	ldy #2	;dereference handle again	lda [@pfxHndl]	sta @tmpPtr	sta bufPtr	lda [@pfxHndl],y	sta @tmpPtr+2	sta bufPtr+2	pla	;retrieve new length of buffer	sta [@tmpPtr]	;store in buffer	bra @try_again	;go try again@got_prefix	ldy #4	;unlock the handle	lda [@pfxHndl],y	asl a	lsr a	sta [@pfxHndl],y		pea 0	;high word of new size allocation	ldy #2	lda [@tmpPtr],y	;get the length of the returned string	clc	adc #4	;include length words	pha	;put on stack for call	pei @pfxHndl+2	pei @pfxHndl	_SetHandleSize	;resize the handle so it's just the right size	ldy @pfxHndl+2	;return handle to caller	ldx @pfxHndl	clc	;no error@exit	pld	;clean up stack frame	pla	pla	pla	pla	rts;############################################################;#;# setPfx - restore prefix to it's original value;#;# on entry:;#    Acc = prefix number;#    X,Y = handle to stored prefix;#;############################################################setPfx@tmpPtr	equ $01	sta prefixNum	;save prefix number in parm block	pha	;make space on stack for temp pointer	pha	tsc	;make stack frame	phd	tcd	;;;	lda #2	;2 parms for SetPrefix call;;;	sta pCount	stx @tmpPtr	sty @tmpPtr+2	ldy #2	;dereference handle to prefix string	lda [@tmpPtr]	;but set pointer to length	clc	;word within buffer	adc #2	sta bufPtr	lda [@tmpPtr],y	adc #0	sta bufPtr+2	_SetPrefixGS parmBlock*** added 5-Feb-92 DAL -- Dispose of the input handle; we're done with it	pei <@tmpPtr+2	pei <@tmpPtr	_DisposeHandle*** end 5-Feb-92	pld	;clean up stack	pla	pla	rtsparmBlockpCount	dc.w 2	;always 2 (GetPrefix and SetPrefix)prefixNum	dc.w 0bufPtr	dc.l 0	EndP******************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************CDevStuff	proc	import HandleActivate	import TheItemPtr********************************************************************************* OpenNewCDevAY** Input:  Pathname in AY*         Pointer to small rectangle on stack** TheItemPtr points to the CDevItem structure, if any (and TheRawCDevNumber* indicates the icon's position in the main list).** Output: TheCDevWindow in AY (NIL if failed to open)********************************************************************************	export OpenNewCDevAY	import StartResourceManager	import StopResourceManager	import AdjustNumCDevsOpen	import GetMyMainMenuID	import GetCDevListOpenNewCDevAY	phb	phk	plb	sta CDevPathname+2	sty CDevPathname	stz TheCDevWindow+2	stz TheCDevWindow	lda 5,s	sta smallRectPtr	lda 7,s	sta smallRectPtr+2	pha	pha	_GetPort	pha	_GetCurResourceApp	pha	_MMStartUp	_SetCurResourceApp	jsl StartResourceManager*** added 6-Feb-92 DAL -- Build the CDev list if we don't already have it	jsl GetCDevList	jsr FindTheItemPtr	lda >TheItemPtr+1	beq @notAlreadyOpen	phd	lda >TheItemPtr+2	pha	lda >TheItemPtr	pha	tsc	tcd	ldy #oCDevItemWindow+2	lda [1],y	tax	dey	dey	lda [1],y	ply	ply	pld	tay	bne @isOpen	txy	beq @notAlreadyOpen@isOpen	sta >TheCDevWindow	tay	txa	sta >TheCDevWindow+2	pha	phy	_SelectWindow	brl @exit@notAlreadyOpen*** end 6-Feb-92	lda CDevPathname+2	ldy CDevPathname	jsr OpenCDevResourceFork	bcc @fine	brl @exit@fine	sta CDEVResNum; A is already	lda CDEVResNum	jsr LoadTheCDev	;resource file number in A	bcs @exit	jsr UpdateFlagsBuffer  ;added 20-Aug-91 DAL	jsr CheckMachine	bcc @machineOk*** Close the CDev file	lda CDevResNum	pha	_CloseResourceFile	jsl StopResourceManager	lda #$ffff	sta >globalErrorCode	bra @exit@machineOK	jsr MakeCDevWindow	;invisible window, sets up refcon	bcs @exit	jsr PushCDevWindPtr	_SetPort	;added 3-Mar-91 DAL	jsr MakeCDevControls	bcs @exit	lda nwContentRect	pha	sec	sbc #13	sta nwContentRect	lda smallRectPtr+1	beq @noWhoosh	pea $8000	pea $0000	;flag: zoom out	pushlong smallRectPtr	pushlong #nwContentRect	_WhooshRect@noWhoosh	pla	sta nwContentRect	jsr PushCDevWindPtr	_ShowWindow	lda #1	jsl AdjustNumCDevsOpen	jsr InstallRunTask	jsr ForceUpdateEvent   ;added 13-Oct-91 DAL@exit	_SetCurResourceApp	_SetPort	pla	plx	ply	ply	;throw away rect ptr	phx	pha	plb	lda >TheCDevWindow	tay	lda >TheCDevWindow+2	rtlCDevPathname	dc.l 0TheCDevWindow	dc.l 0TheRefcon	dc.l 0CDevResNum	dc.w 0smallRectPtr	dc.l 0********************************************************************************* FindTheItemPtr** Inputs:   CDevPathname (pointer to class-one string)**  CDevListCount*  CDevItemsHandle*  CDevPathsHandle** Outputs:  sets >TheItemPtr if we find a CDev item matching this path********************************************************************************	import CDevItemsHandle,CDevPathsHandle,CDevListCountFindTheItemPtr	lda TheItemPtr+1	beq @dontHave	rts@dontHave	phd	pushlong CDevItemsHandle	pushlong CDevPathsHandle	lda CDevListCount	pha	pea 0	tsc	tcd@rawNumber	equ 1@count	equ @rawNumber+2@paths	equ @count+2@items	equ @paths+4	ldy #4	lda [<@paths],y	pha	ora #$8000	sta [<@paths],y	;locked handle	lda [<@items],y	pha	ora #$8000	sta [<@items],y	;locked handle	ldy #2	lda [<@paths],y	tax	lda [<@paths]	sta <@paths	stx <@paths+2	lda [<@items],y	tax	lda [<@items]	sta <@items	stx <@items+2	lda <@count	beq @done@loop	pushlong CDevPathname	ldy #oCDevItemPathOffset	clc	lda [<@items],y	adc <@paths	tax	iny	iny	lda [<@items],y	adc <@paths+2	pha	phx	;pushed this item's pathname	jsr ExpandThisPath	jsr ComparePathnames	bcs @tryNext	lda <@items+2	sta >TheItemPtr+2	lda <@items	sta >TheItemPtr;;;	lda <@rawNumber;;;	jsr FindInSortedList;;;	sta >TheRawCDevNumber	bra @done@tryNext	clc	lda [<@items]	adc <@items	sta <@items	bcc @1	inc <@items+2@1	inc <@rawNumber	dec <@count	bne @loop@done	ldy #4	lda CDevItemsHandle+2	sta <@items+2	lda CDevItemsHandle	sta <@items	pla	sta [<@items],y	;restored lock state	lda CDevPathsHandle+2	sta <@paths+2	lda CDevPathsHandle	sta <@paths	pla	sta [<@paths],y	;restored lock state	pla	;discard raw-number count	pla	;discard count	pla	pla	;discard path ptr	pla	pla	;discard item ptr	pld	rts** ComparePathnames** Input:  two pointers to class-one pathnames, on the stack** Output: BCC if the pathnames match*ComparePathnames	phd	tsc	tcd@one	equ 5@two	equ @one+4	lda [<@one]	cmp [<@two]	sec	bne @done	inc a	tay@compare	lda [<@one],y	jsr @upcase	sta >@cheat+1	lda [<@two],y	jsr @upcase@cheat	cmp #$7777	sec	bne @done	dey	cpy #2	bcs @compare;;;	clc@done	pld	plx	pla	pla	pla	pla	;discard input pointers	phx	rts@upcase	and #$00ff	cmp #$0061	bcc @up	cmp #$007b	bcs @up	and #$00df@up	rts** ExpandThisPath -- input pointer on stack*	import ExpandPathBufferExpandThisPath	lda 3,s	sta epath1	lda 5,s	sta epath1+2	pushlong #ExpandPathParms	pea $200e	;ExpandPathGS	jsl $e100b0	lda #ExpandPathBuffer+2	sta 3,s	lda #^ExpandPathBuffer	sta 5,s	rtsExpandPathParms	dc.w 2	;pcountepath1	dc.l 0	dc.l ExpandPathBuffer	export ExpandPathBufferExpandPathBuffer	dc.w ExpandPathLength+4	ds.b ExpandPathLength+2********************************************************************************* OpenCDevResourceFork** Inputs: AY = pointer to class-one pathname** Output: CLC, A=resource file number*         SEC, A=error code********************************************************************************OpenCDevResourceFork	pha	;space for OpenResourceFile result	pea $7777	;requested access (place-holder)	pushlong #0	;map address	pha	phy	jsl WhatAccessRequest	sta 1+4+4,s	;store over	jsr GetAndFixPrefs	;3-Dec-91 DAL	_OpenResourceFile	jsr RestorePrefs	;3-Dec-91 DAL	plx	bcs @out	;if there's an error, don't kill A	txa@out	rts********************************************************************************* Miscellaneous subroutines********************************************************************************GetAndFixPrefs	_GetSysPrefsGS oldPrefs	lda oldPrefs+2	and #$1fff	;keep the reserved bits	ora #$C000	;turn on Use Volume Mount Dialog		;no Cancel button! 3-Dec-91 DAL	sta myPrefs+2	_SetSysPrefsGS myPrefs	rtsRestorePrefs	php	;3-Dec-91 DAL	pha	;3-Dec-91 DAL	_SetSysPrefsGS oldPrefs	pla	;3-Dec-91 DAL	plp	;3-Dec-91 DAL	rtsoldPrefs	dc.w 1	;1 parameter	dc.w 0	;the old SysPrefsmyPrefs	dc.w 1	dc.w 0	;my modified preferences********************************************************************************* WhatAccessRequest** If the boot file system is AppleShare, return $0001 (read-only).* Otherwise, return $0000 (as-allowed).** This result is used for opening the resource forks.********************************************************************************	export WhatAccessRequestWhatAccessRequest	_DInfoGS infoParms	;get the device name for the boot device	bcs oops	_VolumeGS volParms	;now do a Volume call to get the ID of the boot FST	bcs oops	lda fst_id	;get the ID number of the boot FST	cmp #$000D	;is it AppleShare?	bne local_boot	;no, must have been a local boot	lda #1	;return read-only access	rtllocal_bootoops	lda #0	;as-allowed	rtlinfoParms	dc.w 2	;pCount	dc.w 1	;device number (boot device is ALWAYS device 1)	dc.l devName	;pointer to result buffer for device namedevName	dc.w 36	;buffer lengthdevName2	dc.w 0	;string length	ds.b 32	;buffer for device namevolParms	dc.w 5	;pCount	dc.l devName2	;pointer to device name	dc.l volname	;pointer to volume name buffer	dc.l 0	;total blocks	dc.l 0	;free blocksfst_id	dc.w 0	;FST ID numbervolname	dc.w 36	;buffer lengthvolname2	dc.w 0	;string length	ds.b 32	;string buffer********************************************************************************* LoadTheCDev:** Input: Resource file number in A** LoadResource(rCDevCode,1)** Output: SEC if failure*         CLC if JumpToCDev vector set up********************************************************************************LoadTheCDev	jsr UseOnlyThisFile	pha	;save old file	phx	;and depth	pha	pha	pea rCDevCode	pushlong #1	_LoadResource	sta @error	phd	tsc	tcd	lda [3]	sta JumpToCDev+1	ldy #1	lda [3],y	sta JumpToCDev+2	pld	pla	pla	plx	pla	jsr RestoreOldFile	lda @error	cmp #1	rts@error	dc.w 0********************************************************************************* CallTheCDev** Stack must be set up for transferring control to the CDev:**  LONG  Space for result*  WORD  Message*  LONG  Data1*  LONG  Data2********************************************************************************CallTheCDevJumpToCDev	jml >$777777**************************************************************************************************************************************************************** UseOnlyThisFile** Input:  Resource file number in A** Output:  Current resource file is set, depth is 1*          Previous file in A, previous depth in X********************************************************************************UseOnlyThisFile	pha	pha	;space for cur resource file	_GetCurResourceFile	pha	;space for old depth	pea 1	_SetResourceFileDepth	lda 5,s	;retrieve input	pha	_SetCurResourceFile	plx	;get old depth	pla	;get old file	ply	;throw away copy of input	rts********************************************************************************* RestoreOldFile** Input:  Resource file in A, depth in X********************************************************************************RestoreOldFile	pha	;resource file number	phx	;space for old depth	phx	;new depth	_SetResourceFileDepth	plx	;throw away	_SetCurResourceFile	rts********************************************************************************* LoadTheFlags** LoadResource(rCDevFlags,1), return handle** Input: A = resource file number** Output: handle in AX********************************************************************************LoadTheFlags	jsr UseOnlyThisFile	phx	pha	pha	pha	pea rCDevFlags	pushlong #1	_LoadResource	pla	sta @temp	pla	sta @temp+2	pla	plx	jsr RestoreOldFile	lda @temp+2	ldx @temp	rts@temp	dc.l 0********************************************************************************* CheckMachine--return SEC if the ROM version is bad********************************************************************************IDRoutine	equ $FE1F	;returns ROM version in YCheckMachine	pha	pha	pha	pha	;space for FWEntry results	pha	;a	pha	;x	pha	;y	pea IDRoutine		_FWEntry	ply	plx	pla	pla	sty @ROMVersion	sep #$20	lda flagMachine	cmp @ROMVersion	rep #$20	bcc @ok	beq @ok	rts@ok*** The ROM version is okay--now try calling MachineCDEV to see if*** we should really display this sucker	lda theFlags	and #wantMachine	beq @didMachine	lda #0	pha	pha	pea MachineCDev	pha	pha	pha	pha	jsl CallTheCDev	pla	ply	bne @didMachine	tay	bne @didMachine	sec	rts	;returned zero--don't display@didMachine	clc	rts@ROMVersion	dc.w 0********************************************************************************* MakeCDevWindow--return pointer in TheCDevWindow, SEC if failure** Input: TheItemPtr points to the CDEVItem structure (or NIL if none!)********************************************************************************	import UseStandardPalette,PushMainWindPtr	import ListMemHandle,MainWindPtr,RebuildMemRecMakeCDevWindow	phd	pha	pha	;space for refcon pointer	pushlong CDevPathname	tsc	tcdthePathname	equ 1myRefcon	equ thePathname+4*** Allocate the Refcon storage space	lda [<thePathname]	clc	adc #owbCDevPath	inc a	inc a	;size needed = owbCDevPath + room for pathname	pha	pha	;space for NewHandle result	pea 0	;high word of size	pha	;low word of size	pha	_MMStartUp	;memory id	pea $C000	;attributes	pha	pha	;ignored	_NewHandle	pla	sta myRefcon	pla	sta myRefcon+2	ldy #2	;dereference refcon handle into pointer	lda [<myRefcon],y	tax	lda [<myRefcon]	sta <myRefcon	stx <myRefcon+2*** Zero out the fixed-length part of the Refcon structure	ldy #owbCDevPath	lda #0@zero	sta [<myRefcon],y	dey	dey	bpl @zero*** added 6-Feb-92 DAL -- copy the CDev pathname into the refcon structure	pei <thePathname+2	pei <thePathname	;source	clc	lda <myRefcon	adc #owbCDevPath	tax	lda <myRefcon+2	adc #0	pha	phx	;destination	pea 0	lda [<thePathname]	inc a	inc a	pha	;length	_BlockMove*** end 6-Feb-92*** read the CDev Flags resource into the refcon structure	lda CDevResNum	jsr LoadTheFlags	;takes resource file in A, returns handle in AX	pha	phx	;source for HandToPtr	lda #oCDevItemFlags	jsr PushRefconOffset	pushlong #CDEVITEMSIZE-oCDevItemFlags	_HandToPtr	jsr UpdateFlagsBuffer*** Stuff CDev code resource pointer into the refcon structure	ldy #owbCDevCodePtr	lda JumpToCDev+1	sta [<myRefCon],y	iny	lda JumpToCDev+2	sta [<myRefCon],y*** Stuff the CDev resource file number into the refcon structure	ldy #owbResFileNum	lda CDevResNum	sta [<myRefCon],y*** Stuff the CDEVItem pointer into the refcon structure (this will be NIL if*** the CDev was not in *:System:CDevs when we built the list)	ldy #owbCDevItemPtr	lda >TheItemPtr	sta [<myRefCon],y	iny	iny	lda >TheItemPtr+2	sta [<myRefCon],y	ldy #owbRawCDevNumber	lda >TheRawCDevNumber	sta [<myRefCon],y	jsr BuildWindowTitle	clc	lda <myRefcon	adc #owbWindTitle	sta nwTitle	lda <myRefcon+2	adc #0	sta nwTitle+2*** Removed 6-May-93 DAL;;;	jsl UseStandardPalette	jsr GrabSystemColorTable	jsr GetCDevRectangle	pha	pha	;space for result	pushlong #nwParms	_NewWindow	plx	stx TheCDevWindow	plx	stx TheCDevWindow+2	bcc @noExit	brl @exit@noExit	jsr CreateAuxWindInfo	jsr PushCDevWindPtr	_SetSysWindow*** Set the refcon to point to the window block structure	pei <myRefCon+2	pei <myRefCon	jsr PushCDevWindPtr	_SetWRefCon*** added 6-Feb-92 DAL -- put the window pointer into the CDev item	lda >TheItemPtr+1	bne @haveItem	brl @noItem@haveItem	phd	lda >TheItemPtr+2	pha	lda >TheItemPtr	pha	tsc	tcd	ldy #oCDevItemWindow+2	lda TheCDevWindow+2	sta [1],y	dey	dey	lda TheCDevWindow	sta [1],y*** If the main window exists, update the icon state in the list & inval window	lda MainWindPtr+1	beq @noMainWind*** 7-Feb-92 DAL -- If we just opened something that we have a list entry for, mark it open	lda ListMemHandle+2	ldy ListMemHandle	sta 3	sty 1	ldy #2	lda [1],y	tax	lda [1]	sta 1	stx 3	lda >TheItemPtr	tay	lda >TheItemPtr+2	jsr FindListIndex	pha	pha	;space for _Multiply	pha	;item index	pea LISTMEMSIZE	_Multiply	clc	pla	adc <1	sta <1	pla	adc <3	sta <3	ldy #oMemState	lda [1],y	ora #$0002	;open	sta [1],y*** end 7-Feb-92@noMainWind	pla	pla	pld@noItem*** end 6-Feb-92	clc@exit	pla	pla	pla	pla	pld	rtsnwParms	dc.w nwEnd-nwParms	;length	dc.w $C0C8	;frame (title, close, invisible, qContent)nwTitle	dc.l 0	;title (none yet)	dc.l 0	;refcon	dc.w 0,0,0,0	;zoom rect	dc.l windColorTbl	;color table	dc.w 0,0	;origin	dc.w 0,0	;data height & width	dc.w 1000,1000	;max height & width	dc.w 0,0	;scroll ver & scroll hor	dc.w 0,0	;page ver, page hor	dc.l 0	;info refcon	dc.w 0	;info height	dc.l 0	;defproc	dc.l 0	;no info defproc	dc.l CDevContentDraw ;content defprocnwContentRect	dc.w 40,30,120,590	;position rectangle	dc.l $ffffffff	;plane (front)	dc.l 0	;storagenwEndwindColorTbl	dc.w $0000,$0f00,$020f,$f0f0,$00f0GrabSystemColorTable	pha	pha	;space for LoadResource	pea $8010	;rWindColor	pea $07ff	pea $0001	_LoadResource	plx	ply	bcs @oops	phy	phx	pushlong #windColorTbl	pushlong #10	_HandToPtr@oops	rts********************************************************************************* BuildWindowTitle********************************************************************************BuildWindowTitle	lda #oCDevItemName	jsr PushRefconOffset	lda #owbWindTitle+1	jsr PushRefconOffset	pushlong #16	_BlockMove	ldy #owbWindTitle+1	lda [<myRefcon],y	and #$00ff	inc a	inc a	ora #$2000	dey	sta [<myRefcon],y	clc	and #$00ff	adc #owbWindTitle	tay	lda #$0020	sta [<myRefCon],y	rts	********************************************************************************* PushRefconOffset--push <myRefcon+A under the RTS address********************************************************************************PushRefconOffset	plx	clc	adc <myRefcon	tay	lda <myRefcon+2	adc #0	pha	phy	phx	rts********************************************************************************* CreateAuxWindInfo -- installs the AuxWindInfo data to make the CDev window*                      receive events just like an NDA does.********************************************************************************oNDAStructure	equ 24	;offset into auxWindInfo recordCreateAuxWindInfo	pha	_MMStartUp	pla	sta ndaMemoryID	pha	pha	jsr PushCDevWindPtr	_GetAuxWindInfo	phd	tsc	tcd	ldy #oNDAStructure+2	lda #^TheNDAStructure	sta [3],y	dey	dey	lda #TheNDAStructure	sta [3],y	pld	pla	pla	rts	export TheNDAStructureTheNDAStructure	dc.w 0	;status--not open	dc.l 0	;open proc	dc.l CDevCloseProc	;close	dc.l CDevActionProc	;action	dc.l 0	;init	dc.w 0	;period (reserved)	dc.w $ffff	;mask	dc.l 0	;serviced (reserved)	dc.l 0	;window (reserved)	dc.l 0	;handle (reserved)ndaMemoryID	dc.w 0	;mem id (Desk Manager sets resource app to this!)********************************************************************************* InstallRunTask--install myRunTask in the Run Queue** (If it's already installed, that's okay.)********************************************************************************InstallRunTask	pushlong #myRunTask	_AddToRunQ	rts********************************************************************************* RemoveRunTask--if there are no CDev windows open, remove*                myRunTask from the Run Queue********************************************************************************RemoveRunTask	lda #0	jsl AdjustNumCDevsOpen	tax	bne @someOpen	pushlong #myRunTask	_RemoveFromRunQ@someOpen	rts********************************************************************************* myRunTask -- entered in the Run Queue whenever there are any CDev windows*              open** This calls the CDev run routines********************************************************************************myRunTask	dc.l 0	;link (used by system)	dc.w 60	;period (60 ticks)	dc.w $A55A	;signature	dc.l 0	;reserved for systemmyRunTaskCode	phb	phk	plb*** call doCDevRun for each open CDev window	pha	_GetCurResourceApp	pha	_MMStartUp	;not MyMemID!	_SetCurResourceApp	pha	pha	_GetFirstWindow@tryThisWindow	pha	;space for GetWKind	lda 5,s	pha	lda 5,s	pha	_GetWKind	pla	beq @tryNext	;app window	pha	pha	;space for GetAuxWindInfo	lda 7,s	pha	lda 7,s	pha	_GetAuxWindInfo	phd	tsc	tcd	ldy #24	lda [3],y	tax	iny	iny	lda [3],y	pld	ply	ply	cmp #^TheNDAStructure	bne @tryNext	cpx #TheNDAStructure	bne @tryNext	pushlong TheCDevWindow	lda 3+4,s	sta TheCDevWindow+2	lda 1+4,s	sta TheCDevWindow	jsr RunOneCDev	pulllong TheCDevWindow@tryNext	lda 3,s	pha	lda 3,s	pha	_GetNextWindow	lda 2,s	bne @tryThisWindow	pla	pla	;discard window pointer (now nil)	_SetCurResourceApp@noRunWindow	plb	rtl********************************************************************************* RunOneCDev** Input:  TheCDevWindow********************************************************************************RunOneCDev	jsr PushGlobalStuff	jsr SetupCDevGlobals	jsr GetFlagsFromWindow	lda theFlags	and #wantRun	beq @noRun*** set resource file to this CDev	pha	_GetCurResourceFile	lda CDevResNum	pha	_SetCurResourceFile	pha	pha	_GetPort	jsr PushCDevWindPtr	_SetPort	pha	pha	pea RunCDEV	jsr PushCDevWindPtr	pea 0	pea 0	jsl CallTheCDev	pla	pla	_SetPort	_SetCurResourceFile@noRun	jsr PopGlobalStuff	rts********************************************************************************* PushCDevWindPtr -- push TheCDevWindow under the RTS address********************************************************************************PushCDevWindPtr	plx	pushlong TheCDevWindow	phx	rts********************************************************************************* CDevCloseProc -- close a CDev window********************************************************************************CDevCloseProc	import StopResourceManager,CondDisposeCDevList	import AdjustNumCDevsOpen,cbp	import DeactivateIfNotMyWindowNext	phb	phk	plb*** 28-Oct-92 DAL -- update dalight savings time stuff now (don't wait for DeskShutDown)	jsl cbp*** end 28-Oct-92	jsr GetDeskWindowPtr	jsr SetupCDevGlobals	jsr GetFlagsFromWindow	pha	_GetCurResourceFile	lda CDevResNum	pha	_SetCurResourceFile	lda theFlags	and #wantClose	beq @didClose	pha	pha	_GetPort	jsr PushCDevWindPtr	_SetPort	;preserve port & set the CDev port	pha	pha	pea CloseCDEV	jsr PushCDevWindPtr	;data1=window pointer	pea 0	pea 0	;data2=undefined	jsl CallTheCDEV	pla	pla	_SetPort	;restore old port setting@didClose	jsr SaveWindowLocation	import ClosingCDevWindow	jsr PushCDevWindPtr	jsl ClosingCDevWindow ;fix up data & zoom closed	pha	pha	;space for FindHandle result	pha	pha	;space for GetWRefCon result	jsr PushCDevWindPtr	_GetWRefCon	_FindHandle	_DisposeHandle	;dispose the Window Block	jsr PushCDevWindPtr	_CloseWindow;;;	lda #0;;;	jsl HandleActivate	jsl DeactivateIfNotMyWindowNext	;17-Mar-93 DAL	_SetCurResourceFile	lda CDevResNum	pha	_CloseResourceFile	lda #$ffff	jsl AdjustNumCDevsOpen	;decrement by 1	jsl StopResourceManager	;stop if we're the last one	jsl CondDisposeCDevList	;dispose if we're last (6-Feb-92 DAL)	jsr RemoveRunTask		;remove if we're the last one	plb	rtl********************************************************************************* SaveWindowLocation** Inputs:  PushCDevWindPtr tells us which window we're closing*          CDev's name is at oCDevItemName in the refcon of that window********************************************************************************SaveWindowLocation	lda MainResFile	jsr UseOnlyThisFile	pha	phx	pha	pha	jsr PushCDevWindPtr	_GetWRefCon	clc	pla	adc #oCDevItemName	sta cdevNamePtr	tax	pla	adc #0	sta cdevNamePtr+2*** AX = pointer to CDev name	pha	pha	;space for RMFindNamedResource result	pea rTwoRects	pha	phx	;pushed pointer to name	pushlong #theFileID	_RMFindNamedResource	plx	ply	bcc @gotResourceIDyx	brl @noRectResource@gotResourceIDyx	sty rectResID+2	stx rectResID	pha	pha	;space for LoadResource	pea rTwoRects	phy	phx	_LoadResource	plx	ply	bcc @noProblemo	brl @exit@noProblemo	phy	phx	;re-push rTwoRects handle	phd	tsc	tcd	ldy #2	lda [<3],y	tax	lda [<3]	sta <3	stx <5	;derefed rTwoRects	jsr Bump3by8for640	pha	pha	_GetPort	jsr PushCDevWindPtr	_SetPort	stz theWindPos	stz theWindPos+2	pushlong #theWindPos	_LocalToGlobal	_SetPort	lda theWindPos	cmp [3]	bne @changed	lda theWindPos+2	ldy #2	cmp [3],y	beq @noChange@changed	lda theWindPos	sta [3]	lda theWindPos+2	ldy #2	sta [3],y	pea $ffff	;true (changed)	pea rTwoRects	pushlong rectResID	_MarkResourceChange@noChange	pld	plx	plx	brl @exit*** There was no rTwoRects resource for this CDev, so try creating one@noRectResource	pha	pha	;space for new handle	pushlong #16	;size of rTwoRects	pha	_MMStartUp	;memory ID	pea 0	;attributes	pha	pha	;ignored	_NewHandle	plx	stx rectResHndl	ply	sty rectResHndl+2	phy	phx	;re-push rTwoRects handle	phd	tsc	tcd	ldy #2	lda [<3],y	tax	lda [<3]	sta <3	stx <5	;derefed rTwoRects	ldy #14	lda #0@zeroIt	sta [3],y	dey	dey	bpl @zeroIt	jsr Bump3by8for640	pha	pha	_GetPort	jsr PushCDevWindPtr	_SetPort	ldy #2	lda #0	sta [3],y	sta [3]	pei 5	pei 3	_LocalToGlobal	_SetPort	pushlong rectResHndl ;handle for AddResource	pea 0	;attributes for AddResource	pea rTwoRects	;resource type for AddResource	pha	pha	;space for UniqueResourceID result	pea $0077	;get a rTwoRects($0077xxxx) ID	pea rTwoRects	_UniqueResourceID	lda 3,s	sta rectResID+2	lda 1,s	sta rectResID	_AddResource	bcs @exit0	pea rTwoRects	pushlong rectResID	pushlong cdevNamePtr	_RMSetResourceName@exit0	pld	plx	plx@exit	plx	pla	jsr RestoreOldFile	rtstheFileID	dc.w 0	;result from RMFindNamedResource (who cares?)cdevNamePtr	dc.l 0rectResID	dc.l 0rectResHndl	dc.l 0theWindPos	dc.w 0,0********************************************************************************* CDevActionProc -- action for a CDev window********************************************************************************CDevActionProc	phd	phb	phk	plb	pha	;action = <5	phy	;ptr high = <3	phx	;ptr low = <1	tsc	tcd	jsr PushGlobalStuff*** Fetch window pointer from desk globals	jsr GetDeskWindowPtr	jsr SetupCDevGlobals	jsr GetFlagsFromWindow	pha	_GetCurResourceFile	lda CDevResNum	pha	_SetCurResourceFile	pha	pha	_GetPort	;leave old port on stack	jsr PushCDevWindPtr	_SetPort	lda 5	asl a	tax	cmp #actionEnd-actionTable	bcs @tooBig	lda 5	jsr (actionTable,x)@tooBig	_SetPort	;restore old port	_SetCurResourceFile	;added 1-Apr-91 DAL	jsr PopGlobalStuff	plx	;pull ptr low	plx	;pull ptr high	plx	;pull action	plb	pld	lda #0	;return value	rtlactionTable	dc.w null	;0 = unused	dc.w doCDevEvent	;1 = eventAction	dc.w doCDevRun	;2 = runAction	dc.w doCDevCursor	;3 = cursorAction	dc.w null	;4 = unused	dc.w doCDevUndo	;5 = undoAction	dc.w doCDevCut	;6 = cutAction	dc.w doCDevCopy	;7 = copyAction	dc.w doCDevPaste	;8 = pasteAction	dc.w doCDevClear	;9 = clearActionactionEnd********************************************************************************* PushGlobalStuff** Save important globals on the stack in case we're handling a reentrant* action-routine call.** Stuff we need to save:*   TheCDevWindow*   CDevResNum*   JumpToCDev*   FlagsBuffer..FlagsBufferEnd-1********************************************************************************PushGlobalStuff	ply	lda TheCDevWindow+2	pha	lda TheCDevWindow	pha	lda CDevResNum	pha	lda JumpToCDev+2	pha	lda JumpToCDev+1	pha	ldx #FlagsBufferEnd-FlagsBuffer-2@push	lda FlagsBuffer,x	pha	dex	dex	bpl @push	phy	rts********************************************************************************* PopGlobalStuff (see PushGlobalStuff)********************************************************************************PopGlobalStuff	ply	ldx #0@pop	pla	sta FlagsBuffer,x	inx	inx	cpx #FlagsBufferEnd-FlagsBuffer	bcc @pop	pla	sta JumpToCDev+1	pla	sta JumpToCDev+2	pla	sta CDevResNum	pla	sta TheCDevWindow	pla	sta TheCDevWindow+2	phy	rts********************************************************************************* GetDeskWindPtr********************************************************************************GetDeskWindowPtr	pha	pha	;space for result	pea 0	;0 = get NDA window pointer	_GetDeskGlobal	pla	sta TheCDevWindow	pla	sta TheCDevWindow+2	rtsSetupCDevGlobals	pha	pha	jsr PushCDevWindPtr	_GetWRefCon	phd	tsc	tcd	ldy #owbResFileNum	lda [3],y	sta CDevResNum	ldy #owbCDevCodePtr	lda [3],y	sta JumpToCDev+1	iny	lda [3],y	sta JumpToCDev+2	pld	pla	pla	rts********************************************************************************* Boring actions********************************************************************************doCDevCursor	rts********************************************************************************* Edit actions actions********************************************************************************doCDevUndodoCDevCutdoCDevCopydoCDevPastedoCDevClear	tay	;keep action code in Y	lda theFlags	and #wantEdit	beq @didEdit	pha	pha	;space for result (ignored)	pea EditCDev	pea 0	phy	;data1 = edit action code	jsr PushCDevWindPtr	;data2 = window pointer	jsl CallTheCDev	pla	pla@didEdit	rtsdoCDevRunnull	rts********************************************************************************* ForceUpdateEvent********************************************************************************ForceUpdateEvent	phd	pushlong #myTaskRec	tsc	tcd	lda #updateEvt	sta myTaskWhat	lda TheCDevWindow	sta myTaskMsg	lda TheCDevWindow+2	sta myTaskMsg+2	jsr doCDevEvent@cleanup	pla	pla	pld	rts********************************************************************************* doEvent -- call EventsCDEV, TaskMasterDA, HitCDev********************************************************************************	import SpecialEventHandling,DeactivateIfNotMyWindowNextdoCDevEvent	jsl SpecialEventHandling	;added 15-Jul-92 DAL	jsr SimulateEditEvents	bcs @cont	brl @allThrough@cont*** Feed the event to the CDev if it wants it	lda theFlags	and #wantEvents	beq @didEvent	pha	pha	pea EventsCDev	pei 3	pei 1	;data1 = event record pointer	jsr PushCDevWindPtr	;data2 = window pointer! 11-Jun-91 DAL	jsl CallTheCDev	pla	pla	lda CDevResNum	;1-Apr-91 DAL (Twlight screws up!)	pha	;1-Apr-91 DAL	_SetCurResourceFile	;1-Apr-91 DAL@didEvent	pha	pea $fffe	;disable Menu Help	_MenuGlobal	pla	sta >saveMenuGlobals	pei 3	pei 1	pushlong #myTaskRec	pushlong #16	_BlockMove	pha	;result space	pha	;input mask (ignored)	pushlong #myTaskRec	_TaskMasterDA	pha	lda >saveMenuGlobals;;;	and #$7fff	;restore old menu help setting	asl a	lsr a	;cleared bit 15	pha	_MenuGlobal	pla	;throw away MenuGlobal result	pla	;pull TaskMasterDA result	cmp #activateEvt	bne @notActivate	lda myTaskMods*** added 17-Mar-93 DAL	and #1	bne @normal	jsl DeactivateIfNotMyWindowNext	rts@normal*** end 17-Mar-93	jsl HandleActivate	rts@notActivate	cmp #wInControl	bne @notHit	lda theFlags	and #wantHit	beq @didHit	pha	pha	;space for HitCDEV result	pea HitCDev	pushlong myTaskData2  ;data1=control handle*** push data2 = the control ID, or $FFFFFFFF if this is not an extended control	lda #$ffff	pha	pha	pushlong myTaskData2	_GetCtlID	;data2 = control ID	jsl CallTheCDev	pla	pla	jsr SetupFromBRAM@didHit@notHit@allThrough	rts********************************************************************************* SimulateEditEvents -- use event record at <1, theFlags** If the event is a keypress for an Edit item, call SystemEdit and* return CLC to say we handled it.********************************************************************************SimulateEditEvents	lda theFlags	and #wantEdit	beq @notMe	lda [<1]	;event.what	cmp #3	;keyDownEvt	beq @key	cmp #5	;autoKeyEvt	beq @key@notMe	sec	rts@key	ldy #14	;offset to modifiers	lda [<1],y	and #$0100	;command key?	beq @notMe	ldy #2	;offset to message	lda [<1],y	and #$00ff	cmp #'a'	bcc @notLC	and #$df	;uppercase@notLC	ldx #1	;1 = code for Undo	cmp #'Z'	beq @gotIt	inx	;2 = code for Cut	cmp #'X'	beq @gotIt	inx	;3 = code for Copy	cmp #'C'	beq @gotIt	inx	;4 = code for Paste	cmp #'V'	bne @notMe@gotIt	pha	;space for result	phx	;edit code	_SystemEdit	pla	;discard result	clc	rts*******************************************************************************myTaskRecmyTaskWhat	dc.w 0myTaskMsg	dc.l 0	dc.l 0	;whenmyTaskWhere	dc.w 0,0myTaskMods	dc.w 0myTaskData	dc.l 0myTaskMask	dc.l $001fffff	;everything (5.0.3)	dc.l 0	;lastClickTick	dc.w 0	;click countmyTaskData2	dc.l 0	;task data 2myTaskData3	dc.l 0	;task data 3myTaskData4	dc.l 0	;task data 4	dc.w 0,0	;last click pointsaveMenuGlobals	dc.w 0********************************************************************************* GetCDevRectangle********************************************************************************;;;	import MainResFileGetCDevRectangle	lda flagDataRect+6	sta nwContentRect+6	lda flagDataRect+4	sta nwContentRect+4	lda flagDataRect+2	sta nwContentRect+2	lda flagDataRect	sta nwContentRect	lda theFlags	and #wantRect	beq @didRect	pha	pha	pea RectCDEV	pushlong #nwContentRect	lda #0	pha	pha	jsl CallTheCDev	pla	pla@didRect	jsr CenterTheRect*** if there's a rectangle saved, use it!	pha	_GetCurResourceFile	lda >MainResFile	pha	_SetCurResourceFile	pha	pha	;space for result	pea rTwoRects	lda #oCDevItemName	jsr PushRefconOffset	_RMLoadNamedResource	plx	ply	bcs @exit	phy	phx	;re-push rTwoRects(1) handle	phd	tsc	tcd	ldy #2	lda [<3],y	tax	lda [<3]	sta <3	stx <5	;derefed rTwoRects	jsr Bump3by8for640	ldy #2	lda [3]	ora [3],y	beq @rectIsZero	pushlong #nwContentRect	lda nwContentRect+2	eor #$ffff	inc a	pha	lda nwContentRect	eor #$ffff	inc a	pha	_OffsetRect	pushlong #nwContentRect	ldy #2	lda [3],y	pha	lda [3]	pha	_OffsetRect@rectIsZero	pld	plx	plx	;discard long@exit	_SetCurResourceFile	rtsBump3by8for640	pha	_GetMasterSCB	pla	and #$0080	beq @ok	lda #8	;offset to 640 rectangle	clc	adc <3	sta <3	bcc @ok	inc <5@ok	rts******************************************************************************** CenterTheRect -- if the rectangle is at (0,0) still,*                  move it somewhere near center-screen********************************************************************************CenterTheRect	lda nwContentRect	ora nwContentRect+2	bne @TopLeftNotZero	pushlong #nwContentRect	jsr PushXOffset	jsr PushYOffset	_OffsetRect	@TopLeftNotZero	rtsPushXOffset	pha	_GetMasterSCB	pla	ldx #640	and #$0080	bne @gotRes	ldx #320@gotRes	sec	lda nwContentRect+6	sbc nwContentRect+2	sta @temp	txa	sec	sbc @temp	lsr a	plx	pha	phx	rts@temp	dc.w 0PushYOffset	sec	lda nwContentRect+4	sbc nwContentRect	cmp #200-23	bcc @ok	lda #200-23@ok	eor #$ffff	inc a	clc	adc #200-23	lsr a	clc	adc #23	plx	pha	phx	rts********************************************************************************* CDevContentDraw -- bank register not set!********************************************************************************CDevContentDraw	pha	_GetCurResourceFile*** Get resource file number from owbResFileNum in refcon structure	pha	pha	;space for GetWRefCon	pha	pha	;space for GetPort	_GetPort	_GetWRefCon	phd	tsc	tcd	ldy #owbResFileNum	lda [3],y	pld	plx	plx	;discard refcon pointer	pha	_SetCurResourceFile	pha	pha	_GetPort	_DrawControls	_SetCurResourceFile	rtl********************************************************************************* MakeCDevControls** Let the CDev create all its controls********************************************************************************MakeCDevControls	lda theFlags	and #wantCreate	beq @createByResource	pha	pha	pea CreateCDEV	jsr PushCDevWindPtr	;data1=window pointer	lda #0	pha	pha	;data2=undefined	jsl CallTheCDev	pla	pla	bra @didCreate** wantCreate is off, so we will create controls from the CDev's* rControlList ID = 1 resource.*@createByResource	pha	pha	;space for result	jsr PushCDevWindPtr	pea 9	;resourceToResource	pushlong #1	;ID=1	_NewControl2	pla	pla	;(ignore result)@didCreate	jsr HideAllControls	lda theFlags	and #wantInit	beq @didInit	pha	pha	pea InitCDev	jsr PushCDevWindPtr	;data1=window pointer	lda #0	pha	pha	;data2=undefined	jsl CallTheCDev	pla	pla@didInit	jsr ShowAllControls	clc	rts********************************************************************************* HideAllControls********************************************************************************HideAllControls	sec	bra ShowHideAll********************************************************************************* ShowAllControls********************************************************************************ShowAllControls	clcShowHideAll	ror HideFlag	pha	pha	;space for oneCtlHandle	jsr PushCDevWindPtr	_GetWControls	phd	tsc	tcdoneCtl	equ 3@while	lda <oneCtl+1	;is this a NIL handle?	beq @done	jsr FollowPointer	;now it's a pointer	ldy #$10	;offset to ctlFlag	lda [<oneCtl],y	and #$ff7f	;make it visible		bit HideFlag	bpl @noHide	ora #$0080	;whoops, make it invisible@noHide	sta [<oneCtl],y	jsr FollowPointer	;now it's the next handle	bra @while@done	pld	pla	pla	rts********************************************************************************* FollowPointer** This routine is used for 2 things:*   1. To deref a control handle into a control pointer*   2. To "deref" a control pointer into the next control handle.*      (Since the ctlNext field is first in the record, this is*       the same thing.)********************************************************************************FollowPointer	ldy #2	lda [<oneCtl],y	tax	lda [<oneCtl]	sta <oneCtl	stx <oneCtl+2	rtsHideFlag	dc.w 0********************************************************************************* SetupFromBRAM** If the updateSSFromBRAM flag bit is set, call ToBRAMSetup with SEC.** 27-Jan-92 DAL: No longer need to force Bank to $00 (patched ToBramSetup*                vector in 6.0d66).********************************************************************************SetupFromBRAM	lda theFlags	and #updateSSFromBRAM	beq @didBRAM;;;	phb;;;	pea 0;;;	plb;;;	plb	php	sep #$30	sec	jsl ToBRAMSetup	plp;;;	plb@didBRAM	rts********************************************************************************* UpdateFlagsBuffer********************************************************************************UpdateFlagsBuffer	lda CDevResNum	jsr LoadTheFlags	pha	phx	pushlong #FlagsBuffer	pushlong #FlagsBufferEnd-FlagsBuffer	_HandToPtr	rts********************************************************************************* GetFlagsFromWindow********************************************************************************GetFlagsFromWindow	pha	pha	jsr PushCDevWindPtr	_GetWRefCon	pla	plx	clc	adc #oCDevItemFlags	bcc @1	inx@1	phx	pha	pushlong #FlagsBuffer	pushlong #FlagsBufferEnd-FlagsBuffer	_BlockMove	rts********************************************************************************* FlagsBuffer holds a copy of the current rCDevFlags(1) resource********************************************************************************FlagsBuffertheFlags	dc.w 0flagEnabled	dc.b 0flagVersion	dc.b 0flagMachine	dc.b 0flagReserved	dc.b 0flagDataRect	dc.w 0,0,0,0flagName	ds.b 16flagAuthor	ds.b 33flagVersionStr	ds.b 9FlagsBufferEnd*******************************************************************************	EndP********************************************************************************* Crude Palette Manager** Entry points:*   HandleActivate--calls UseStandardPalette or RestorePalette*                   (Input: A = modifiers field from activate)*   UseStandardPalette*   RestorePalette** Call these on Activate and Deactivate of a window that needs to use the* standard colors for the current mode.********************************************************************************HandleActivate	proc export	lsr a	bcc RestorePalette	export UseStandardPaletteUseStandardPalette	lda >MyPaletteActive	bne @alreadyActive	lda #1	sta >MyPaletteActive	pha	pha	;space for result	pea $000f	;table number to use	lda #0	pha	pha	;table pointer = NIL	pea $8000	;use 640 colors even in 320 mode;	_UseColorTable	ldx #$1612	jsl $e10000	pla	sta >ColorInfoHandle	pla	sta >ColorInfoHandle+2@alreadyActive	rtlRestorePalette	phb	phk	plb	lda MyPaletteActive	beq @notActive	lda IgnoreTheDeactivate	stz IgnoreTheDeactivate	bne @ignore		stz MyPaletteActive	pushlong ColorInfoHandle	pea $0000	;flags;	_RestoreColorTable	ldx #$1712	jsl $e10000@ignore@notActive	plb	rtl********************************************************************************* DeactivateIfNotMyWindowNext** Calls HandleActivate(A=deactivate) *if* the front window is NOT mine,* because if the front window *is* mine then we can just keep the cool* color table instead of reverting to the application colors, and then* re-instating my cool colors again, which is really icky to watch.********************************************************************************	export DeactivateIfNotMyWindowNextDeactivateIfNotMyWindowNext	import TheNDAStructure	pha	pha	_FrontWindow	plx	ply	bne @notNIL	txa	beq @isNIL@notNIL	tya	cmp >MainWindPtr+2	bne @notMain	txa	cmp >MainWindPtr	beq @isMine@notMain	pha	pha	;space for GetAuxWindInfo	phy	phx	;window pointer for GetAuxWindInfo	_GetAuxWindInfo	phd	tsc	tcd	ldy #24	lda [3],y	tax	iny	iny	lda [3],y	pld	ply	ply	cmp #^TheNDAStructure	bne @notMine	cpx #TheNDAStructure	beq @isMine@isNIL@notMine	lda #0	jsl HandleActivate@isMine	rtl	export IgnoreOneDeactivateIgnoreOneDeactivate	lda >IgnoreTheDeactivate	inc a	sta >IgnoreTheDeactivate	rtlMyPaletteActive	dc.w 0ColorInfoHandle	dc.l 0IgnoreTheDeactivate	dc.w 0	EndP	end